-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part coa1 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa1-cases-seat.l4: cases for coa1-seat.l4. Each case is the set of facts a real person in the seat would state, asked of one
-- seat question, with the answer decided by reading the quoted words of the section before the run (never copied from the output).
-- Dates and pound amounts are illustrative inputs, not figures from the Act. Arguments follow the GIVEN order of each question.

-- ---- Part 2 ----
-- Dana and Eli are subscribing their names to a memorandum and have complied with ss 9 to 13: "A company is formed under this Act by one or more persons— (a) subscribing their names ... and (b) complying with the requirements"
#ASSERT `Under section 7(1), is the company formed under this Act` 2 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Nobody has subscribed: one or more persons are needed, and the section does not say what follows otherwise
#ASSERT `Under section 7(1), is the company formed under this Act` 0 TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "A company may not be so formed for an unlawful purpose."
#ASSERT `Under section 7(2), may we form the company for this purpose` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 7(2), may we form the company for this purpose` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Our company will have a share capital and the memorandum states every point
#ASSERT `Under section 8(1), is our document a memorandum of association` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The memorandum says nothing about each subscriber taking a share, and the company is to have a share capital
#ASSERT `Under section 8(1), is our document a memorandum of association` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "The memorandum must be in the prescribed form and must be authenticated by each subscriber."
#ASSERT `Under section 8(2), does our memorandum meet the requirements as to form and authentication` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 8(2), does our memorandum meet the requirements as to form and authentication` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 8(2), does our memorandum meet the requirements as to form and authentication` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "The memorandum ... must be delivered to the registrar together with an application for registration ..., the documents required by this section and a statement of compliance."
#ASSERT `Under section 9(1), have we delivered to the registrar everything the section requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 9(1), have we delivered to the registrar everything the section requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 9(2), does our application state what it must` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 9(2), does our application state what it must` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "If the application is delivered by a person as agent ..., it must state his name and address." We deliver it ourselves.
#ASSERT `Under section 9(3), does our application give the agent's name and address as required` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 9(3), does our application give the agent's name and address as required` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 9(3), does our application give the agent's name and address as required` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No subscriber is disqualified, so (c) and (d) of s 9(3A) bind nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 9(3A), does our application contain the statements about the subscribers it must contain` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- One subscriber would be disqualified but for a court's permission, and the application does not give the details
#ASSERT `Under section 9(3A), does our application contain the statements about the subscribers it must contain` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A company limited by guarantee, with no share capital
#ASSERT `Under section 9(4), does our application contain the statements of capital, guarantee, officers and significant control it must` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A company to have a share capital whose application has no statement of capital
#ASSERT `Under section 9(4), does our application contain the statements of capital, guarantee, officers and significant control it must` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 9(5), does our application contain the registered office, email, articles and company-type statements it must` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The intended registered office address is not an appropriate address: "which must be an appropriate address within the meaning given by section 86(2)"
#ASSERT `Under section 9(5), does our application contain the registered office, email, articles and company-type statements it must` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- We propose our own articles and have not enclosed a copy
#ASSERT `Under section 9(5), does our application contain the registered office, email, articles and company-type statements it must` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 9(6), which registrar must we deliver our application to` `Scotland` EQUALS "the registrar of companies for Scotland"
#ASSERT `Under section 9(6), which registrar must we deliver our application to` `England and Wales` EQUALS "the registrar of companies for England and Wales"
#ASSERT `Under section 9(6), which registrar must we deliver our application to` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS "the registrar of companies for Northern Ireland"
-- "(1) The required information about a subscriber who is an individual is— (a) name; (b) a service address."
#ASSERT `Under section 9A, what information must we give about a subscriber` `an individual` FALSE EQUALS JUST (LIST `s 9A the individual's name`, `s 9A a service address`)
-- A subscriber that is a registered company: "corporate or firm name; a service address"
#ASSERT `Under section 9A, what information must we give about a subscriber` `a company registered under the Companies Act 2006` FALSE EQUALS JUST (LIST `s 9A the corporate or firm name`, `s 9A a service address`)
-- A partnership that is not a legal person: the section is silent
#ASSERT `Under section 9A, what information must we give about a subscriber` `a partnership` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A peer, usually known by a title: "that title may be stated ... instead of the subscriber’s forename and surname"
#ASSERT `Under section 9A(4), is the name we give for a subscriber acceptable` TRUE "Lord Brown" "Peter" "Brown" "Lord Brown" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 9A(4), is the name we give for a subscriber acceptable` FALSE "Lord Brown" "Peter" "Brown" "Lord Brown" EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The statement of capital and initial shareholdings states every item for every class
#ASSERT `Under section 10(2), does our statement of capital and initial shareholdings state what it must` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 10(2), does our statement of capital and initial shareholdings state what it must` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 10(4), does our statement state what it must for each subscriber` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 10(4), does our statement state what it must for each subscriber` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A subscriber is to take shares of two classes: "the information required under subsection (4)(a) is required for each class"
#ASSERT `Under section 10(5), is the share information given for each class a subscriber takes` 2 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 10(5), is the share information given for each class a subscriber takes` 2 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 10(5), is the share information given for each class a subscriber takes` 1 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 11(3), does our statement of guarantee state what it must` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 11(3), does our statement of guarantee state what it must` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I am a member of a guarantee company and the company is wound up while I am a member
#ASSERT `Under section 11(3), does a member's guarantee undertaking apply to me if the company is wound up` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I left on 1 March 2024: winding up began on 1 March 2025 (exactly one year) and on 2 March 2025 (a day later)
#ASSERT `Under section 11(3), does a member's guarantee undertaking apply to me if the company is wound up` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 11(3), does a member's guarantee undertaking apply to me if the company is wound up` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 2 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- debts 100 + costs 50 + adjustment 20 = 170, specified amount 150: the specified amount is the ceiling
#ASSERT `Under section 11(3), what is the most I can be required to contribute on a winding up, in pounds` TRUE 100 50 20 150 EQUALS JUST 150
#ASSERT `Under section 11(3), what is the most I can be required to contribute on a winding up, in pounds` TRUE 100 50 20 1000 EQUALS JUST 170
#ASSERT `Under section 12(1), does our statement of proposed officers contain the required information about the first officers` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A public company must name a first secretary
#ASSERT `Under section 12(1), does our statement of proposed officers contain the required information about the first officers` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 12(2A), does our statement confirm that each individual named as a director has a verified identity` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 12(2A), does our statement confirm that each individual named as a director has a verified identity` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The statement confirms the identity is verified but it is not in fact verified: the text is silent
#ASSERT `Under section 12(2A), does our statement confirm that each individual named as a director has a verified identity` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 12(3), does our statement include the subscribers' statement that each proposed officer has consented to act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 12(3), does our statement include the subscribers' statement that each proposed officer has consented to act` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 12(4), does our statement include the subscribers' statement that no proposed director is disqualified or ineligible` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 12(4), does our statement include the subscribers' statement that no proposed director is disqualified or ineligible` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Someone will be a registrable person on incorporation and the statement gives the particulars
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(1), does our statement of initial significant control state what it must` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Nobody will be a registrable person, and the statement says so
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(1), does our statement of initial significant control state what it must` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Someone will be a registrable person and the statement omits the particulars
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(1), does our statement of initial significant control state what it must` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(1A), does our statement include the further statements it must where there is a registrable person` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(1A), does our statement include the further statements it must where there is a registrable person` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(1A), does our statement include the further statements it must where there is a registrable person` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(3), does our statement say the particulars of an individual are included with the individual's knowledge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(3), does our statement say the particulars of an individual are included with the individual's knowledge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(3), does our statement say the particulars of an individual are included with the individual's knowledge` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 12B(2), may our statement include a statement that a registrable person's identity is verified` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 12B(2), may our statement include a statement that a registrable person's identity is verified` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 12B(4), is our application accompanied by the individual's confirmation that they are a relevant officer` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 12B(4), must our application come with the individual's confirmation that they are a relevant officer` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the question asked whether the application MUST come with the confirmation, but the function answers whether it IS accompanied (JUST TRUE accompanied, JUST FALSE required but not accompanied, NOTHING where no statement under s 12B(3) is included); retitled to ask that, facts and expected value unchanged
#ASSERT `Under section 12B(4), is our application accompanied by the individual's confirmation that they are a relevant officer` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 12B(4), must our application come with the individual's confirmation that they are a relevant officer` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE; the question asked whether the application MUST come with the confirmation, but the function answers whether it IS accompanied (JUST TRUE accompanied, JUST FALSE required but not accompanied, NOTHING where no statement under s 12B(3) is included); retitled to ask that, facts and expected value unchanged
#ASSERT `Under section 12B(4), is our application accompanied by the individual's confirmation that they are a relevant officer` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 12B(4), must our application come with the individual's confirmation that they are a relevant officer` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING; the question asked whether the application MUST come with the confirmation, but the function answers whether it IS accompanied (JUST TRUE accompanied, JUST FALSE required but not accompanied, NOTHING where no statement under s 12B(3) is included); retitled to ask that, facts and expected value unchanged
#ASSERT `Under section 13(2), may the registrar accept our statement of compliance as sufficient evidence that the registration requirements are met` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 13(2), may the registrar accept our statement of compliance as sufficient evidence that the registration requirements are met` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "If the registrar is satisfied that the requirements of this Act as to registration are complied with, he shall register the documents delivered to him."
#ASSERT `Under section 14, must the registrar register the documents we delivered` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 14, must the registrar register the documents we delivered` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 15(1), must the registrar give us a certificate that the company is incorporated` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 15(1), will the registrar give us a certificate that the company is incorporated` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE; the question asked whether the registrar WILL give a certificate (a prediction), but the function states the registrar's duty on registration ("shall give"); retitled to ask whether the registrar must, facts and expected value unchanged
-- Our company's liability is limited to the amount unpaid on the shares: the certificate must say it is limited by shares
#ASSERT `Under section 15(2), what must our certificate of incorporation say about our members' liability` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` EQUALS JUST `s 15(2)(c) that the company is a limited company limited by shares`
#ASSERT `Under section 15(2), what must our certificate of incorporation say about our members' liability` `liability not limited` EQUALS JUST `s 15(2)(c) that the company is an unlimited company`
#ASSERT `Under section 15(2), what must our certificate of incorporation say about our members' liability` `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up` EQUALS JUST `s 15(2)(c) that the company is a limited company limited by guarantee`
-- Our liability is limited in some other way by the constitution: the text provides only for shares and guarantee
#ASSERT `Under section 15(2), what must our certificate of incorporation say about our members' liability` `liability limited in some other way by the constitution` EQUALS NOTHING
-- An unlimited company's certificate need not say by shares or guarantee
#ASSERT `Under section 15(2), does our certificate of incorporation state what it must` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `liability not limited` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A company limited by shares whose certificate omits "by shares or by guarantee"
#ASSERT `Under section 15(2), does our certificate of incorporation state what it must` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "The certificate must be signed by the registrar or authenticated by the registrar's official seal."
#ASSERT `Under section 15(3), is our certificate of incorporation signed or sealed as required` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 15(3), is our certificate of incorporation signed or sealed as required` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 15(3), is our certificate of incorporation signed or sealed as required` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 15(4), is our certificate conclusive evidence that the company is duly registered` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 15(4), is our certificate conclusive evidence that the company is duly registered` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The company was incorporated on 1 March 2026 ("as from the date of incorporation")
#ASSERT `Under section 16(1), have the effects of registration begun on this date` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 16(1), have the effects of registration begun on this date` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I am a subscriber and the date is the date of incorporation
#ASSERT `Under section 16(2), am I one of the body corporate that registration creates` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I am a member who joined later; asked about a date before incorporation
#ASSERT `Under section 16(2), am I one of the body corporate that registration creates` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 16(5), how many shares do I hold on registration as a subscriber` TRUE TRUE 100 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `Under section 16(5), how many shares do I hold on registration as a subscriber` TRUE FALSE 100 EQUALS NOTHING
-- I am named as director in the statement of proposed officers: "deemed to have been appointed ... unless ineligible"
#ASSERT `Under section 16(6), am I deemed to have been appointed to the office I am named for on registration` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 16(6), am I deemed to have been appointed to the office I am named for on registration` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- Part 3 ----
-- Our articles are our constitution
#ASSERT `Under section 17, is this document part of the company's constitution` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A Chapter 3 resolution is part of the constitution
#ASSERT `Under section 17, is this document part of the company's constitution` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A document that is neither: "include" does not close the list
#ASSERT `Under section 17, is this document part of the company's constitution` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A company limited by shares need not register articles (model articles apply by s 20); an unlimited company must
#ASSERT `Under section 18(2), must our company register articles of association` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 18(2), must our company register articles of association` `liability not limited` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 18(3), do our registered articles meet the requirements as to form` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 18(3), do our registered articles meet the requirements as to form` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A limited company that registered no articles: the model articles form part of its articles so far as applicable
#ASSERT `Under section 20(1), does a provision of the model articles form part of our articles` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Our registered articles exclude that provision
#ASSERT `Under section 20(1), does a provision of the model articles form part of our articles` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An unlimited company is not a limited company
#ASSERT `Under section 20(1), does a provision of the model articles form part of our articles` `liability not limited` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 21(1), may we amend our articles by this resolution` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 21(1), may we amend our articles by this resolution` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A charity in England and Wales: sections 197 and 198 of the Charities Act 2011
#ASSERT `Under section 21(2), what other enactments limit our power to amend our articles` TRUE FALSE `England and Wales` EQUALS LIST `s 21 sections 197 and 198 of the Charities Act 2011`
#ASSERT `Under section 21(2), what other enactments limit our power to amend our articles` FALSE FALSE `England and Wales` EQUALS EMPTY
-- "Provision for entrenchment may only be made— (a) in the company's articles on formation, or (b) by an amendment ... agreed to by all the members"
#ASSERT `Under section 22(2), may we make provision for entrenchment in this way` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 22(2), may we make provision for entrenchment in this way` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 22(3), does provision for entrenchment prevent this amendment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 22(3), does provision for entrenchment prevent this amendment` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 23(1), must we give the registrar notice that our articles contain or are restricted by entrenchment` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 23(1), must we give the registrar notice that our articles contain or are restricted by entrenchment` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 23(2), must we give the registrar notice that entrenchment or a restriction has been removed` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 23(2), must we give the registrar notice that entrenchment or a restriction has been removed` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Our articles contain entrenchment and we are amending them and must send the registrar a document
#ASSERT `Under section 24(2), must we deliver a statement of compliance with the document making the amendment` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 24(2), must we deliver a statement of compliance with the document making the amendment` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 24(3), is our statement the statement of compliance required` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 24(3), is our statement the statement of compliance required` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I became a member before the alteration, which requires me to hold 11 shares when I hold 10 and I have not agreed: "is not bound"
#ASSERT `Under section 25(1), am I protected from being bound by an alteration of the articles` TRUE 11 10 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The alteration requires exactly the shares I hold: nothing in (a) or (b)
#ASSERT `Under section 25(1), am I protected from being bound by an alteration of the articles` TRUE 10 10 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I agreed in writing to be bound
#ASSERT `Under section 25(1), am I protected from being bound by an alteration of the articles` TRUE 11 10 FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The amendment took effect on 1 March 2026: "not later than 15 days after" is 16 March 2026
#ASSERT `Under section 26(1), did we send the registrar the amended articles in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 26(1), did we send the registrar the amended articles in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 17 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 26(3), do I commit an offence as an officer if our company did not send the amended articles in time` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I am an officer who is not in default: the text names only "every officer of the company who is in default"
#ASSERT `Under section 26(3), do I commit an offence as an officer if our company did not send the amended articles in time` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 26(3), do I commit an offence as an officer if our company did not send the amended articles in time` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "one-tenth of level 3" with level 3 taken, for this test, as 1000 pounds
#ASSERT `Under section 26(4), what is the most I can be fined for continued contravention each day, in pounds` 1000 EQUALS 100
-- The registrar's notice was issued on 1 March 2026; we complied on 29 March 2026 (28 days) or on 30 March 2026
#ASSERT `Under section 27(4), is our company liable to a civil penalty if it ignored the registrar's notice` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 29 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 27(4), is our company liable to a civil penalty if it ignored the registrar's notice` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 27(4), is our company liable to a civil penalty if it ignored the registrar's notice` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 27(3), can criminal proceedings still be brought if we complied with the registrar's notice in time` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 29 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 27(3), can criminal proceedings still be brought if we complied with the registrar's notice in time` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 28(1), is a provision that was in our memorandum before Part 3 began now treated as part of our articles` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 28(1), is a provision that was in our memorandum before Part 3 began now treated as part of our articles` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A special resolution: Chapter 3 applies
#ASSERT `Under section 29(1), does Chapter 3 apply to this resolution or agreement` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An ordinary resolution that is none of (b) to (e)
#ASSERT `Under section 29(1), does Chapter 3 apply to this resolution or agreement` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 30(1), what must we forward to the registrar about a resolution or agreement` TRUE EQUALS `s 30(1) a copy of the resolution or agreement`
#ASSERT `Under section 30(1), what must we forward to the registrar about a resolution or agreement` FALSE EQUALS `s 30(1) a written memorandum setting out the terms of the resolution or agreement`
#ASSERT `Under section 30(1), did we forward it to the registrar in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 30(1), did we forward it to the registrar in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 17 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 30(2), do I commit an offence as an officer if our company did not forward it in time` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 30(2), do I commit an offence as an officer if our company did not forward it in time` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 31(1), are our company's objects unrestricted` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 31(1), are our company's objects unrestricted` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "the amendment is not effective until entry of that notice on the register": the bar stands until entry
#ASSERT `Under section 31(2), is our amendment of the statement of objects still not effective` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 31(2), is our amendment of the statement of objects still not effective` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 32(1), must the company send me its constitutional documents on my request` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 32(1), must the company send me its constitutional documents on my request` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A company limited by shares with a share capital and no other documents: articles, certificates, statement of capital
#ASSERT `Under section 32(1), which documents must the company send me` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `s 32(1)(a) an up-to-date copy of the company's articles`, `s 32(1)(f) a copy of the company's current certificate of incorporation, and of any past certificates`, `s 32(1)(g) a current statement of capital`
-- A guarantee company without a share capital: articles, certificates, statement of guarantee
#ASSERT `Under section 32(1), which documents must the company send me` `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `s 32(1)(a) an up-to-date copy of the company's articles`, `s 32(1)(f) a copy of the company's current certificate of incorporation, and of any past certificates`, `s 32(1)(h) a copy of the statement of guarantee`
#ASSERT `Under section 33(1), is the party bound by the company's constitution as if by covenants` Member EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 33(1), is the party bound by the company's constitution as if by covenants` Company EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 33(1), is the party bound by the company's constitution as if by covenants` Creditor EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 33(2), is money I owe the company under its constitution a debt` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 34(2), did we give the registrar notice in time that an enactment altered our constitution` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 34(2), did we give the registrar notice in time that an enactment altered our constitution` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 17 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 34(3), what must come with our notice that an enactment altered our constitution` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS LIST `s 34(2) a copy of the special enactment`, `s 34(3) a copy of the company's articles as amended`
#ASSERT `Under section 35(1), did we give the registrar notice in time that a court order altered our constitution` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 35(1), did we give the registrar notice in time that a court order altered our constitution` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 17 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 35(2), what must come with our notice that a court order altered our constitution` FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `s 35(2)(a) a copy of the order`
-- A copy of a resolution still in force and not yet written into the articles must accompany each copy of the articles we issue
#ASSERT `Under section 36(1), must this document or statement accompany a copy of our articles that we issue` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Its effect has been written into the articles by amendment
#ASSERT `Under section 36(1), must this document or statement accompany a copy of our articles that we issue` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- three occasions at level 3 (1000 pounds for this test): "for each occasion"
#ASSERT `Under section 36(4), what is the most I can be fined for the occasions copies were issued or requested, in pounds` 1000 3 EQUALS 3000
-- A guarantee company with no share capital: a profit-sharing right outside membership is void
#ASSERT `Under section 37, is a provision in our articles giving a right to profits otherwise than as a member void` `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same provision in a company limited by shares: the section is for guarantee companies without a share capital
#ASSERT `Under section 37, is a provision in our articles giving a right to profits otherwise than as a member void` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 38, does an enactment or rule of law for companies with several members apply to our one-member company` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 38, does an enactment or rule of law for companies with several members apply to our one-member company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- Part 4 ----
-- A non-charity company in England: the act is challenged for lack of capacity under the constitution: "shall not be called into question"
#ASSERT `Under section 39(1), can the validity of the company's act be called into question for lack of capacity` TRUE `England and Wales` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A charity company, I knew it was a charity and gave no consideration: section 42 takes the act out of section 39
#ASSERT `Under section 39(1), can the validity of the company's act be called into question for lack of capacity` TRUE `England and Wales` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A charity company, and I did not know it was a charity: section 39 still applies in my favour
#ASSERT `Under section 39(1), can the validity of the company's act be called into question for lack of capacity` TRUE `England and Wales` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
