-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part coa3 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa3-cases-seat.l4: cases for the seat layer coa3-seat.l4. Each case gives the facts a real person in the seat would state,
-- and the answer the TEXT gives, decided by hand from the section named in the question before the code was run.
-- A question with no limit on the answer asserts every kind of answer the section can give: JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING (not covered).

-- Aisha signed the memorandum and the company has been registered: she is a member from registration (s 112(1))
#ASSERT `Under section 112, am I a member of the company` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Ben agreed to become a member and his name is entered in the register (s 112(2))
#ASSERT `Under section 112, am I a member of the company` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Carys signed the memorandum but the company is not yet registered: not yet a member
#ASSERT `Under section 112, am I a member of the company` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Dev agreed to become a member but his name is not yet entered: the text does not say he is not a member
#ASSERT `Under section 112, am I a member of the company` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Eli is entered as a member with his name in the wrong form (s 112(4)): membership is preserved
#ASSERT `Under section 112(4), do I still become a member although my name is entered in the wrong form` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 112(4), does the wrong form of my name in the register stop me being a member` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE; the old name asked whether the wrong form stops me being a member, but s 112(4) and the function answer the opposite (JUST TRUE means I do still become a member); retitled to ask what the function answers
-- Fay is entered in the right form: s 112(4) is not engaged
#ASSERT `Under section 112(4), do I still become a member although my name is entered in the wrong form` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 112(4), does the wrong form of my name in the register stop me being a member` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the old name asked whether the wrong form stops me being a member, but s 112(4) and the function answer the opposite (JUST TRUE means I do still become a member); retitled to ask what the function answers
-- Gus asks about a company registered under the Act
#ASSERT `Under section 113(1), must the company keep a register of its members` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Gus asks about a body that is not a company under the Act
#ASSERT `Under section 113(1), must the company keep a register of its members` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Hana ceased to be a member last year
#ASSERT `Under section 113(2A), must the register show the date I stopped being a member` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Hana is still a member
#ASSERT `Under section 113(2A), must the register show the date I stopped being a member` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
