-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part coa4 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa4-cases-seat.l4: cases for the seat questions of coa4-seat.l4 (Companies Act 2006, ss 154 to 204(2)). Each case states the facts a
-- real person in the seat would give, in the order of the question's inputs, and the answer the TEXT gives (written by reading the section
-- named, before the code was run). JUST TRUE = yes, JUST FALSE = no, NOTHING = the Act does not say on these facts (a "not covered" case).
-- Where a seat answer is a number of pounds the figures for the standard scale are invented for the case (the Act does not state them).


-- ---- Chapter 1: Requirement to have directors (ss 154 to 156) ----
-- s 154(1): a private company must have at least one director; one is enough
#ASSERT `Under section 154, does my company have enough directors` FALSE 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a private company with none
#ASSERT `Under section 154, does my company have enough directors` FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 154(2): a public company must have at least two directors
#ASSERT `Under section 154, does my company have enough directors` TRUE 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a public company with one
#ASSERT `Under section 154, does my company have enough directors` TRUE 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 155(1): at least one director must be a natural person
#ASSERT `Under section 155, does my company have a director who is a natural person` 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 155, does my company have a director who is a natural person` 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 155(2): the office held by a natural person as a corporation sole meets the requirement
#ASSERT `Under section 155, does my company have a director who is a natural person` 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 155(2): or otherwise by virtue of an office
#ASSERT `Under section 155, does my company have a director who is a natural person` 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 156(1): if the company appears to be in breach of s 154
#ASSERT `Under section 156, may the Secretary of State direct my company to appoint a director` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- or of s 155
#ASSERT `Under section 156, may the Secretary of State direct my company to appoint a director` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- NOT COVERED: neither appears; s 156(1) gives the power on that appearance and does not say the Secretary of State may not otherwise
