-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part coa6 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa6-cases-seat.l4: cases for the seat layer coa6-seat.l4 (Companies Act 2006, Part 12, ss 270 to 280).
-- Each case is a person in the seat stating facts, and the answer the text of the section gives. The expected value was decided
-- from the section (line numbers in ukpga-2006-46.txt) before the encoding was run, and is written beside the assertion.
-- Answers: JUST TRUE is the Act's yes, JUST FALSE its no in its own words, NOTHING "not covered" (never read NOTHING as no).
-- The pounds used for "level 4" and "level 5" are ILLUSTRATIONS: the Act does not say what a level stands for.
-- Company-type facts are written in the order the questions ask them: the certificate says "public"?, how the members' liability
-- is limited, a share capital?, the registration requirements complied with on or after the relevant date?

§ `Cases: the seat's questions`

-- A public limited company (a plc): its certificate says so, its members' liability is limited by shares, it has a share capital, and
-- the registration requirements were complied with. A private limited company (a Ltd): its certificate does not say it is public.
`s 270 case liability limited by shares` MEANS `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held`

-- ---- s 270 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 270(1) "A private company is not required to have a secretary": the director of a Ltd asks; the director of a plc gets no answer.
#ASSERT `Under section 270(1), is my company required to have a secretary, if it is a private company` FALSE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 270(1), is my company required to have a secretary, if it is a private company` TRUE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a company whose certificate says "public" but whose registration requirements were not complied with is not a public company (s 4(2)(b)),
-- so it is a private company (s 4(1)) and s 270(1) answers no for it
#ASSERT `Under section 270(1), is my company required to have a secretary, if it is a private company` TRUE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- an unlimited private company with no share capital: still a private company
#ASSERT `Under section 270(1), is my company required to have a secretary, if it is a private company` FALSE `liability not limited` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 270(2): a Ltd with no secretary is "without a secretary"; with one it is "with a secretary"; a plc is neither.
#ASSERT `Under section 270(2), is my company a private company without a secretary` FALSE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 270(2), is my company a private company without a secretary` FALSE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 270(2), is my company a private company without a secretary` TRUE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 270(2), is my company a private company with a secretary` FALSE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 270(2), is my company a private company with a secretary` FALSE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 270(3)(a)(i): a Ltd with no secretary may be served direct, for a thing that was to be sent to its secretary.
#ASSERT `Under section 270(3)(a)(i), does the subsection let a thing that the law requires or lets people send to my company's secretary be given or sent to, or served on, my company itself` FALSE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the Ltd has a secretary: outside the subsection's own gate
#ASSERT `Under section 270(3)(a)(i), does the subsection let a thing that the law requires or lets people send to my company's secretary be given or sent to, or served on, my company itself` FALSE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `Under section 270(3)(a)(i), does the subsection let a thing that the law requires or lets people send to my company's secretary be given or sent to, or served on, my company itself` FALSE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING`; name-test sweep, group (i): the gate "In the case of a private company without a secretary" is the text's own, so outside it the answer is JUST FALSE
-- a plc: outside the subsection's own gate
#ASSERT `Under section 270(3)(a)(i), does the subsection let a thing that the law requires or lets people send to my company's secretary be given or sent to, or served on, my company itself` TRUE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `Under section 270(3)(a)(i), does the subsection let a thing that the law requires or lets people send to my company's secretary be given or sent to, or served on, my company itself` TRUE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING`; name-test sweep, group (i): the gate "In the case of a private company without a secretary" is the text's own, so outside it the answer is JUST FALSE
-- s 270(3)(a)(ii): the same thing, addressed to the secretary, is treated as addressed to the company
#ASSERT `Under section 270(3)(a)(ii), is a thing addressed to my company's secretary treated as addressed to my company` FALSE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 270(3)(a)(ii), is a thing addressed to my company's secretary treated as addressed to my company` FALSE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 270(3)(b): I am a director of a Ltd with no secretary, and a notice must be given by the secretary: I may give it
#ASSERT `Under section 270(3)(b), does the subsection let me do or receive, in place of my company's secretary, anything else that the law requires or lets the secretary do or receive` FALSE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I am not a director but the directors have authorised me
#ASSERT `Under section 270(3)(b), does the subsection let me do or receive, in place of my company's secretary, anything else that the law requires or lets the secretary do or receive` FALSE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- neither a director nor authorised: the subsection does not answer
#ASSERT `Under section 270(3)(b), does the subsection let me do or receive, in place of my company's secretary, anything else that the law requires or lets the secretary do or receive` FALSE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the thing is one that (a) deals with: (b) says "anything else"
#ASSERT `Under section 270(3)(b), does the subsection let me do or receive, in place of my company's secretary, anything else that the law requires or lets the secretary do or receive` FALSE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 271 and s 272 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#ASSERT `Under section 271, must my company have a secretary` TRUE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 271, must my company have a secretary` FALSE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a plc with no secretary is in breach of s 271; one with a secretary is not; a Ltd is outside the section
#ASSERT `Under section 271, is my company in breach of the requirement to have a secretary` TRUE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 271, is my company in breach of the requirement to have a secretary` TRUE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 271, is my company in breach of the requirement to have a secretary` FALSE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 272(1): a power of the Secretary of State
#ASSERT `Under section 272(1), may the Secretary of State give my company a direction to appoint a secretary` TRUE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 272(1), may the Secretary of State give my company a direction to appoint a secretary` TRUE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 272(1), may the Secretary of State give my company a direction to appoint a secretary` FALSE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 272(2) and (3): the direction my company received
#ASSERT `Under section 272(2), does the direction my company received state and specify what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 272(2), does the direction my company received state and specify what the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 272(2), is the period the direction gives my company within the limits the subsection sets (not less than one month and not more than three months after the date the direction is given)` (Date 15 3 2024) (Date 15 4 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 272(2), is the period the direction gives my company within the limits the subsection sets (not less than one month and not more than three months after the date the direction is given)` (Date 15 3 2024) (Date 14 4 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 272(2), is the period the direction gives my company within the limits the subsection sets (not less than one month and not more than three months after the date the direction is given)` (Date 15 3 2024) (Date 16 6 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 272(3), does the direction my company received inform it of the consequences of failing to comply` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 272(3), does the direction my company received inform it of the consequences of failing to comply` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 272(4) and (5): the duty to comply
#ASSERT `Under section 272(4), must my company comply with the direction by making the necessary appointment and giving notice of it before the end of the period` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 272(4), must my company comply with the direction by making the necessary appointment and giving notice of it before the end of the period` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 272(5), must my company comply with the direction by giving notice of the appointment before the end of the period` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 272(5), must my company comply with the direction by giving notice of the appointment before the end of the period` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A direction given on 15 March 2024 to a plc with no secretary, giving until 15 May 2024. Arguments: in breach when given?, appointment
-- already made?, made since?, the day made, notice given?, the day given, the last day, today.
-- appointed on 20 March and notice given on 25 March: complied
#ASSERT `Under section 272(4) and (5), has my company complied with the direction` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 20 3 2024) TRUE (Date 25 3 2024) (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 26 3 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- appointed but notice not given, and the last day has passed: not complied
#ASSERT `Under section 272(4) and (5), has my company complied with the direction` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 20 3 2024) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 16 5 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the same, with a month still to run: not yet decided
#ASSERT `Under section 272(4) and (5), has my company complied with the direction` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 20 3 2024) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 15 4 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the plc had already appointed a secretary before the direction: only the notice is needed
#ASSERT `Under section 272(4) and (5), has my company complied with the direction` FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 1 4 2024) (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 2 4 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the notice came one day after the last day
#ASSERT `Under section 272(4) and (5), has my company complied with the direction` FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 16 5 2024) (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 20 5 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 272(6)(a): the company commits an offence if it fails to comply
#ASSERT `Under section 272(6)(a), does my company commit an offence by failing to comply with the direction` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 272(6)(a), does my company commit an offence by failing to comply with the direction` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 272(6)(b): arguments: my company failed?, I am a director?, a manager?, the secretary?, a shadow director?, I am in default?
#ASSERT `Under section 272(6)(b), do I commit an offence as an officer of my company that failed to comply with the direction` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a director who did all he reasonably could: the section names officers in default only
#ASSERT `Under section 272(6)(b), do I commit an offence as an officer of my company that failed to comply with the direction` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the secretary in default
#ASSERT `Under section 272(6)(b), do I commit an offence as an officer of my company that failed to comply with the direction` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a shadow director in default is treated as an officer
#ASSERT `Under section 272(6)(b), do I commit an offence as an officer of my company that failed to comply with the direction` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a person who is none of those: the section does not name them
#ASSERT `Under section 272(6)(b), do I commit an offence as an officer of my company that failed to comply with the direction` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the company complied: no offence for anyone
#ASSERT `Under section 272(6)(b), do I commit an offence as an officer of my company that failed to comply with the direction` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 272(7): the penalty (illustrative pounds: level 5 = 100,000; level 4 = 3,000 or 8,000)
#ASSERT `Under section 272(7), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for the offence, in pounds` 100000 EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `Under section 272(7), on the first wording (one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale), what is the most the daily default fine can be, in pounds` 100000 EQUALS JUST 10000
#ASSERT `Under section 272(7), on the second wording (one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale), what is the most the daily default fine can be, in pounds` 3000 EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `Under section 272(7), on the second wording (one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale), what is the most the daily default fine can be, in pounds` 8000 EQUALS JUST 800

-- ---- s 273 -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#ASSERT `Under section 273(1), are the directors of my company under a duty to take all reasonable steps to secure a suitably qualified secretary` TRUE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 273(1), are the directors of my company under a duty to take all reasonable steps to secure a suitably qualified secretary` FALSE `s 270 case liability limited by shares` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
