-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part coa8 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa8-cases-seat.l4: cases for the seat questions of coa8-seat.l4 (Companies Act 2006, ss 362 to 414B), one or more for every question.
-- Each case gives the facts a person in the seat would state, and the answer written by hand from the text before the run.
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE: the Act says yes, or says no in its own words. NOTHING: the Act does not decide the case on those facts ("not covered").
-- A case marked NOT COVERED asserts NOTHING on purpose: it is the case the text leaves open.


§ `Companies Act 2006, Part 14: control of political donations and expenditure`


§§ `Which parties and organisations the Part covers, and what a political donation and political expenditure are (ss 363 to 365)`

-- A company asks whether a party registered with the Electoral Commission is one it needs authority to give to.
#ASSERT `Under section 363, is this political party one to which the political donations rules apply` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 363, is this political party one to which the political donations rules apply` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- NOT COVERED: a person who is not standing at an election; the text names only candidates at an election to public office, so it is silent on anyone else.
#ASSERT `Under section 363, do the political donations rules apply to this independent election candidate` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 363, do the political donations rules apply to this independent election candidate` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A campaign group that carries on activities meant to affect support for a covered party, or to influence a referendum.
#ASSERT `Under section 363, is this organisation a political organisation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 363, is this organisation a political organisation` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 363, is this organisation a political organisation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 363, is this organisation a political organisation` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
