-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part coa9 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa9-cases-seat.l4: cases for the seat layer. Each case states the facts a real person in the seat would state, and the expected answer was decided from the
-- text of the section named before the code was run (lines 5418-5894 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). JUST TRUE means the section says yes, JUST FALSE that it says no in its
-- own words (or by a choice in NOTES.md), NOTHING that the section does not decide.
-- Amounts: the statutory maximum is taken as 5,000 pounds and level 3 as 1,000 pounds, level 4 as 2,500 and level 5 as 5,000 pounds, as stated INPUTS of the cases:
-- the Act does not state them.

-- ---- Strategic report: a director's questions -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- a director whose report has both items
#ASSERT (`Under section 414C(2), does my strategic report contain a fair review of the company's business and a description of the principal risks and uncertainties?` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the description of principal risks is missing
#ASSERT (`Under section 414C(2), does my strategic report contain a fair review of the company's business and a description of the principal risks and uncertainties?` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the review is what 414C(3) describes
#ASSERT (`Under section 414C(3), is the review in my strategic report the balanced and comprehensive analysis that the section requires?` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the director judges the analysis not balanced and comprehensive
#ASSERT (`Under section 414C(3), is the review in my strategic report the balanced and comprehensive analysis that the section requires?` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- financial key performance indicators are necessary
#ASSERT (`Under section 414C(4)(a), must the review in my strategic report include analysis using financial key performance indicators?` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not necessary: "to the extent necessary" leaves the section silent
#ASSERT (`Under section 414C(4)(a), must the review in my strategic report include analysis using financial key performance indicators?` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- necessary and appropriate
#ASSERT (`Under section 414C(4)(b), must the review in my strategic report include analysis using other key performance indicators?` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not appropriate: "where appropriate" fails
#ASSERT (`Under section 414C(4)(b), must the review in my strategic report include analysis using other key performance indicators?` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- appropriate but not necessary
#ASSERT (`Under section 414C(4)(b), must the review in my strategic report include analysis using other key performance indicators?` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a medium-sized company is excused from the non-financial part of subsection (4)
#ASSERT (`Under section 414C(6), is the review in my company's strategic report excused from the non-financial part of subsection (4) because my company qualifies as medium-sized?` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not medium-sized: "Where a company qualifies as medium-sized" fails
#ASSERT (`Under section 414C(6), is the review in my company's strategic report excused from the non-financial part of subsection (4) because my company qualifies as medium-sized?` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a quoted company: the main trends and factors
#ASSERT (`Under section 414C(7), must the strategic report of my quoted company include this kind of information?` TRUE TRUE "trends") EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- social, community and human rights issues
#ASSERT (`Under section 414C(7), must the strategic report of my quoted company include this kind of information?` TRUE TRUE "social") EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not necessary for an understanding
#ASSERT (`Under section 414C(7), must the strategic report of my quoted company include this kind of information?` TRUE FALSE "employees") EQUALS NOTHING
