-- the directors are not of that opinion
#ASSERT (`Under section 414C(14), does section 414C require my company to disclose information about impending developments or matters in the course of negotiation that the directors think would be seriously prejudicial to the company's interests?` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the report includes a statement describing how the directors had regard to section 172(1)(a) to (f)
#ASSERT (`Under section 414CZA(1), does my strategic report include the section 172(1) statement that the section requires?` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the statement does not describe it
#ASSERT (`Under section 414CZA(1), does my strategic report include the section 172(1) statement that the section requires?` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no statement is included
#ASSERT (`Under section 414CZA(1), does my strategic report include the section 172(1) statement that the section requires?` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a medium-sized company is excused
#ASSERT (`Under section 414CZA(2), is my company excused from including a section 172(1) statement in its strategic report because it qualifies as medium-sized?` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not medium-sized: the "if" fails
#ASSERT (`Under section 414CZA(2), is my company excused from including a section 172(1) statement in its strategic report because it qualifies as medium-sized?` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a parent company whose group had more than 500 million in aggregate net turnover
