-- a later accounts meeting
#ASSERT (`Under section 439A(1)(a), must my quoted company give notice of the intention to move a resolution approving the directors' remuneration policy at this accounts meeting?` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT (`Under section 439A(1)(a), must my quoted company give notice of the intention to move a resolution approving the directors' remuneration policy at this accounts meeting?` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING; a later accounts meeting: outside the first financial year that begins on or after the day the company becomes quoted, a period the text fixes in its own words (fork F35; the other reading is NOTHING)
-- not a quoted company
#ASSERT (`Under section 439A(1)(a), must my quoted company give notice of the intention to move a resolution approving the directors' remuneration policy at this accounts meeting?` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the last financial year of the three
#ASSERT (`Under section 439A(1)(b), is this meeting held no later than the end of the period of three financial years after the last notice?` 5 8) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the year after the period ends
#ASSERT (`Under section 439A(1)(b), is this meeting held no later than the end of the period of three financial years after the last notice?` 5 9) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the section 439 resolution was not passed and no notice was given
#ASSERT (`Under section 439A(2), must my quoted company give notice of a resolution approving the remuneration policy at an accounts meeting?` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- it was passed
#ASSERT (`Under section 439A(2), must my quoted company give notice of a resolution approving the remuneration policy at an accounts meeting?` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a quoted company
#ASSERT (`Under section 439A(2), must my quoted company give notice of a resolution approving the remuneration policy at an accounts meeting?` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a resolution was not passed and no notice was given
#ASSERT (`Under section 439A(2A), must my quoted company give notice of a resolution approving the remuneration policy at an accounts or other general meeting?` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- notice was given
#ASSERT (`Under section 439A(2A), must my quoted company give notice of a resolution approving the remuneration policy at an accounts or other general meeting?` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- notice given prior to the meeting to the entitled members
#ASSERT (`Under section 439A(5), was notice of the policy resolution given as the subsection requires?` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not given
#ASSERT (`Under section 439A(5), was notice of the policy resolution given as the subsection requires?` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a resolution to which the section applies
#ASSERT (`Under section 439A(5), was notice of the policy resolution given as the subsection requires?` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- default; an officer in default
#ASSERT (`Under section 440(1), do I commit an offence as an officer in default because notice of the resolution was not given?` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- default; not in default
#ASSERT (`Under section 440(1), do I commit an offence as an officer in default because notice of the resolution was not given?` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- no default
#ASSERT (`Under section 440(1), do I commit an offence as an officer in default because notice of the resolution was not given?` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not put to the vote; an existing director
#ASSERT (`Under section 440(2), do I commit an offence as an existing director because the resolution was not put to the vote?` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not an existing director
#ASSERT (`Under section 440(2), do I commit an offence as an existing director because the resolution was not put to the vote?` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- put to the vote
#ASSERT (`Under section 440(2), do I commit an offence as an existing director because the resolution was not put to the vote?` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- charged, and proves all reasonable steps
#ASSERT (`Under section 440(3), does the Act give me a defence on these facts?` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- charged, but cannot prove them: this section gives no defence on these facts
#ASSERT (`Under section 440(3), does the Act give me a defence on these facts?` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not charged under subsection (2)
#ASSERT (`Under section 440(3), does the Act give me a defence on these facts?` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale
#ASSERT (`Under section 440(4), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for that offence, in pounds?` 1000) EQUALS JUST 1000

-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part coa10 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa10-cases-seat.l4: cases for the seat layer coa10-seat.l4 (Companies Act 2006, ss 441-474), asked as a director, a company
-- secretary or a member would state the facts. Every expected value was written down from the text of the provision the question
-- names (line numbers in ukpga-2006-46.txt, cited in coa10-seat.l4) before the seat layer was run; none is copied from its output.
-- Each question is asked at least twice, on both sides of its rule where the rule has two sides, and once more where the Act is silent
-- (NOTHING) where some input can make the answer NOTHING. Case dates, amounts and names are invented for the test.

-- ---- question 1: Under section 441(2), must the directors deliver the accounts and reports for the financial year to the registrar ----
-- neither exemption: the directors must deliver (s 441(1))
#ASSERT `Under section 441(2), must the directors deliver the accounts and reports for the financial year to the registrar` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- unlimited company exempt under s 448
#ASSERT `Under section 441(2), must the directors deliver the accounts and reports for the financial year to the registrar` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- dormant subsidiary exempt under s 448A
#ASSERT `Under section 441(2), must the directors deliver the accounts and reports for the financial year to the registrar` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- ---- question 2: Under section 441(1), which of sections 443A to 447 sets out the accounts and reports required of the directors of my company ----
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was the question `Under section 441(1), which section of Chapter 10 sets out the accounts and reports the directors must deliver`; retitled by the second seat-question audit (subject: Chapter 10 also holds ss 448 to 453, and the function names only one of ss 443A to 447; "must deliver" was a consequence the function does not compute); the cases below are unchanged except where marked
-- a micro-entity (second text)
#ASSERT `Under section 441(1), which of sections 443A to 447 sets out the accounts and reports required of the directors of my company` `s 441 second text in the file` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 441 section 443A`
-- a small company with the directors-report exemption
#ASSERT `Under section 441(1), which of sections 443A to 447 sets out the accounts and reports required of the directors of my company` `s 441 second text in the file` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 441 section 444`
-- a small company, first text
#ASSERT `Under section 441(1), which of sections 443A to 447 sets out the accounts and reports required of the directors of my company` `s 441 first text in the file` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 441 section 444`
-- a medium-sized company
#ASSERT `Under section 441(1), which of sections 443A to 447 sets out the accounts and reports required of the directors of my company` `s 441 second text in the file` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 441 section 445`
-- a large unquoted company
#ASSERT `Under section 441(1), which of sections 443A to 447 sets out the accounts and reports required of the directors of my company` `s 441 second text in the file` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 441 section 446`
-- a quoted company
#ASSERT `Under section 441(1), which of sections 443A to 447 sets out the accounts and reports required of the directors of my company` `s 441 second text in the file` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `s 441 section 447`
-- first text: a micro-entity is reached by both 443A and 444, and the text does not say which governs
#ASSERT `Under section 441(1), which of sections 443A to 447 sets out the accounts and reports required of the directors of my company` `s 441 first text in the file` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- ---- question 3: Under section 441(1), does the filing section that applies to my company make it a duty, a permission or not required for the directors to deliver this document to the registrar ----
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was the question `Under section 441(1), must or may the directors deliver this document under the filing section that applies to my company`; retitled by the second seat-question audit (subject: the function answers one of must, may or not required; "must or may" left out the third answer); the cases below are unchanged except where marked
-- small company, annual accounts
#ASSERT `Under section 441(1), does the filing section that applies to my company make it a duty, a permission or not required for the directors to deliver this document to the registrar` `s 441 second text in the file` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 441 annual accounts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 441 the directors must deliver it`
-- medium-sized company exempt from audit: no auditor's report
#ASSERT `Under section 441(1), does the filing section that applies to my company make it a duty, a permission or not required for the directors to deliver this document to the registrar` `s 441 second text in the file` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `s 441 auditor's report` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 441 the section does not require it`
-- quoted company: remuneration report
#ASSERT `Under section 441(1), does the filing section that applies to my company make it a duty, a permission or not required for the directors to deliver this document to the registrar` `s 441 second text in the file` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `s 441 directors' remuneration report` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 441 the directors must deliver it`
-- medium-sized: section 445 does not name the balance sheet as a document
#ASSERT `Under section 441(1), does the filing section that applies to my company make it a duty, a permission or not required for the directors to deliver this document to the registrar` `s 441 second text in the file` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `s 441 balance sheet` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- ---- question 4: Under section 441(1), were the accounts and reports delivered before the end of the period for filing ----
-- private company, delivered on the last day (30 Sep 2026)
#ASSERT `Under section 441(1), were the accounts and reports delivered before the end of the period for filing` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 31 12 2025) FALSE (Date 5 6 2010) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) TRUE (Date 30 9 2026) (Date 1 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- delivered a day late
#ASSERT `Under section 441(1), were the accounts and reports delivered before the end of the period for filing` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 31 12 2025) FALSE (Date 5 6 2010) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) TRUE (Date 1 10 2026) (Date 1 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not delivered and the period is over
#ASSERT `Under section 441(1), were the accounts and reports delivered before the end of the period for filing` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 31 12 2025) FALSE (Date 5 6 2010) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 1 10 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not delivered, but 30 Sep 2026 is the last day: not yet decided
#ASSERT `Under section 441(1), were the accounts and reports delivered before the end of the period for filing` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 31 12 2025) FALSE (Date 5 6 2010) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 30 9 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- extension past the twelve-month limit: the text does not say what it achieves
#ASSERT `Under section 441(1), were the accounts and reports delivered before the end of the period for filing` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 31 12 2025) FALSE (Date 5 6 2010) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) TRUE (Date 2 1 2027) TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- ---- question 5: Under section 442(1), on what date does the period for filing the accounts and reports end ----
-- private, ordinary
#ASSERT `Under section 442(1), on what date does the period for filing the accounts and reports end` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 31 12 2025) FALSE (Date 5 6 2010) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 9 2026)
-- public, ordinary
#ASSERT `Under section 442(1), on what date does the period for filing the accounts and reports end` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 31 12 2025) FALSE (Date 5 6 2010) TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 6 2026)
-- first period of thirteen months, private
#ASSERT `Under section 442(1), on what date does the period for filing the accounts and reports end` (Date 10 1 2024) (Date 31 1 2025) TRUE (Date 10 1 2024) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 10 2025)
-- shortened by a notice dated 1 Jul 2026
#ASSERT `Under section 442(1), on what date does the period for filing the accounts and reports end` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 31 12 2025) FALSE (Date 5 6 2010) FALSE TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 10 2026)
-- extended to the limit
#ASSERT `Under section 442(1), on what date does the period for filing the accounts and reports end` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 31 12 2025) FALSE (Date 5 6 2010) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) TRUE (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 12 2026)
-- extension past the limit
#ASSERT `Under section 442(1), on what date does the period for filing the accounts and reports end` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 31 12 2025) FALSE (Date 5 6 2010) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) TRUE (Date 2 1 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
-- ---- question 6: Under section 442(2), on what date does the period for filing end for an ordinary accounting reference period ----
-- private: nine months
#ASSERT `Under section 442(2), on what date does the period for filing end for an ordinary accounting reference period` (Date 31 12 2025) FALSE EQUALS (Date 30 9 2026)
-- public: six months
#ASSERT `Under section 442(2), on what date does the period for filing end for an ordinary accounting reference period` (Date 31 12 2025) TRUE EQUALS (Date 30 6 2026)
-- last day of April: last day of January (s 443(3))
#ASSERT `Under section 442(2), on what date does the period for filing end for an ordinary accounting reference period` (Date 30 4 2025) FALSE EQUALS (Date 31 1 2026)
-- ---- question 7: Under section 442(3), on what date does the period for filing end for a first accounting reference period of more than twelve months ----
-- private, first period longer than a year
#ASSERT `Under section 442(3), on what date does the period for filing end for a first accounting reference period of more than twelve months` (Date 10 1 2024) (Date 31 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS (Date 10 10 2025)
-- public
#ASSERT `Under section 442(3), on what date does the period for filing end for a first accounting reference period of more than twelve months` (Date 10 1 2024) (Date 31 1 2025) TRUE EQUALS (Date 10 7 2025)
-- ---- question 8: Under section 442(3), is the accounting reference period a period of more than twelve months ----
-- twelve months exactly is not more than twelve months
#ASSERT NOT `Under section 442(3), is the accounting reference period a period of more than twelve months` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 31 12 2025)
-- a year and a day
#ASSERT `Under section 442(3), is the accounting reference period a period of more than twelve months` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 1 1 2026)
-- ---- question 9: Under section 442(4), on what date does the period for filing end, allowing for any notice under section 392 that shortened the accounting reference period ----
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was the question `Under section 442(4), on what date does the period for filing end where the accounting reference period was shortened by a notice under section 392`; retitled by the second seat-question audit (subject: the name stated the shortening as a given, but the function tests it and returns the ordinary period when there is none); the cases below are unchanged except where marked
-- three months from the notice expires last
#ASSERT `Under section 442(4), on what date does the period for filing end, allowing for any notice under section 392 that shortened the accounting reference period` (Date 30 9 2026) TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS (Date 1 10 2026)
-- the base expires last
#ASSERT `Under section 442(4), on what date does the period for filing end, allowing for any notice under section 392 that shortened the accounting reference period` (Date 30 9 2026) TRUE (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS (Date 30 9 2026)
-- no notice
#ASSERT `Under section 442(4), on what date does the period for filing end, allowing for any notice under section 392 that shortened the accounting reference period` (Date 30 9 2026) FALSE (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS (Date 30 9 2026)
-- ---- question 10: Under section 442(5), leaving aside the limit in subsection (5A), may the Secretary of State extend the period for filing on my application ----
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was the question `Under section 442(5), may the Secretary of State extend the period for filing`; retitled by the second seat-question audit (subject: the function does not apply the twelve-month limit of s 442(5A), which the name left unsaid); the cases below are unchanged except where marked
-- applied on the last day
#ASSERT `Under section 442(5), leaving aside the limit in subsection (5A), may the Secretary of State extend the period for filing on my application` (Date 30 9 2026) (Date 30 9 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- applied after the period ended
#ASSERT `Under section 442(5), leaving aside the limit in subsection (5A), may the Secretary of State extend the period for filing on my application` (Date 30 9 2026) (Date 1 10 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the Secretary of State sees no special reason
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `Under section 442(5), may the Secretary of State extend the period for filing` (Date 30 9 2026) (Date 1 9 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; name-test sweep: the layer-1 function behind this question is named for a grant ("may") and answered JUST FALSE because an "If" gate failed; the text does not close the gate with "only if", so a failed gate is NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 442(5), leaving aside the limit in subsection (5A), may the Secretary of State extend the period for filing on my application` (Date 30 9 2026) (Date 1 9 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
