-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part coa16 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa16-cases-seat.l4: cases for coa16-seat.l4, one or more per question, in the facts a person in the seat would state.
-- Every expected value is written from the text beside the assertion, never from the code's output.
-- The money figures (what level 3 or the statutory maximum stands for, the euro equivalent) are made-up inputs: the Act states none.
-- Inputs follow each question's GIVEN order; groups of inputs follow coa16-seat.l4.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Debentures: what a debenture is, and registering an allotment (ss 738 to 742)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- A holder is shown debenture stock that charges no assets: still a debenture ("whether or not constituting a charge").
#ASSERT `Under section 738, is this instrument a debenture for the purposes of the Companies Acts` `s 738 debenture stock` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Shares: the text does not say whether "any other securities of a company" reaches them.
#ASSERT `Under section 738, is this instrument a debenture for the purposes of the Companies Acts` `s 738 a share in a company` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not in a provision of the Companies Acts: the definition is limited to them.
#ASSERT `Under section 738, is this instrument a debenture for the purposes of the Companies Acts` `s 738 a bond` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- A trust deed condition that makes the debentures irredeemable.
#ASSERT `Under section 739(1), is a condition in my debentures, or in the deed securing them, invalid only because the debentures are irredeemable or redeemable only on a contingency or after a period` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Debentures redeemable in some other way: the text is silent.
#ASSERT `Under section 739(1), is a condition in my debentures, or in the deed securing them, invalid only because the debentures are irredeemable or redeemable only on a contingency or after a period` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `Under section 740, may a contract to take up and pay for a company's debentures be enforced by an order for specific performance` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 740, may a contract to take up and pay for a company's debentures be enforced by an order for specific performance` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Debentures allotted on 15 January 2023: two months on is 15 March 2023.
#ASSERT `Under section 741(1), by what date must the company register an allotment of debentures` (Date 15 1 2023) EQUALS Date 15 3 2023
-- Registered on 10 March as soon as practicable: in time.
#ASSERT `Under section 741(1), has the company registered the allotment of debentures as the section requires` (Date 15 1 2023) TRUE (Date 10 3 2023) TRUE (Date 20 3 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Registered on 16 March: one day late.
#ASSERT `Under section 741(1), has the company registered the allotment of debentures as the section requires` (Date 15 1 2023) TRUE (Date 16 3 2023) TRUE (Date 20 3 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not yet registered and it is 1 March: the two months are not up, so no answer yet.
#ASSERT `Under section 741(1), has the company registered the allotment of debentures as the section requires` (Date 15 1 2023) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 1 3 2023) EQUALS NOTHING

-- The company, registered late.
#ASSERT `Under section 741(2), has the company, or have I as an officer of the company, committed an offence by not registering an allotment of debentures in time` (Date 15 1 2023) TRUE (Date 16 3 2023) TRUE (Date 20 3 2023) `coa16 seat the company` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A director who is in default, registered late.
#ASSERT `Under section 741(2), has the company, or have I as an officer of the company, committed an offence by not registering an allotment of debentures in time` (Date 15 1 2023) TRUE (Date 16 3 2023) TRUE (Date 20 3 2023) `coa16 seat me, as an officer of the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A director who is not in default: outside "every officer of the company who is in default".
#ASSERT `Under section 741(2), has the company, or have I as an officer of the company, committed an offence by not registering an allotment of debentures in time` (Date 15 1 2023) TRUE (Date 16 3 2023) TRUE (Date 20 3 2023) `coa16 seat me, as an officer of the company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A shareholder who is not an officer: the text names the company and its officers.
#ASSERT `Under section 741(2), has the company, or have I as an officer of the company, committed an offence by not registering an allotment of debentures in time` (Date 15 1 2023) TRUE (Date 16 3 2023) TRUE (Date 20 3 2023) `coa16 seat me, in some other capacity` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Registered in time: no failure to comply.
#ASSERT `Under section 741(2), has the company, or have I as an officer of the company, committed an offence by not registering an allotment of debentures in time` (Date 15 1 2023) TRUE (Date 10 3 2023) TRUE (Date 20 3 2023) `coa16 seat the company` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Level 3 on the standard scale (a made-up 200 pounds here): the first-conviction ceiling, and one-tenth of it a day.
#ASSERT `Under section 741(3), what is the most the court can fine, in pounds, on a conviction for not registering an allotment of debentures in time` 200 EQUALS JUST 200
#ASSERT `Under section 741(3), what is the most the court can fine, in pounds for each day, as the daily default fine for continued contravention` 200 EQUALS JUST 20

#ASSERT `Under section 742, are debentures to bearer issued in Scotland valid and binding according to their terms` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 742, are debentures to bearer issued in Scotland valid and binding according to their terms` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

