#ASSERT `Under section 767(3), does the company's contravention of section 761 affect the validity of a transaction it entered into` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- A director then in office; the company failed to comply within 21 days (day 22).
#ASSERT `Under section 767(4), am I jointly and severally liable, with the other directors, to indemnify the other party to a transaction the company entered into without a trading certificate` TRUE FALSE 22 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a director when the company entered into it.
#ASSERT `Under section 767(4), am I jointly and severally liable, with the other directors, to indemnify the other party to a transaction the company entered into without a trading certificate` TRUE FALSE 22 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The company complied on day 21.
#ASSERT `Under section 767(4), am I jointly and severally liable, with the other directors, to indemnify the other party to a transaction the company entered into without a trading certificate` TRUE TRUE 21 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part coa17 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa17-cases-seat.l4: cases for the seat layer (coa17-seat.l4): one or more per question, with the facts a real person in the
-- seat would state. Every expected value is decided by reading the section named in the question, written beside the
-- assertion, and never taken from the code's output. Dates and pounds that the Act does not give are marked as illustrative
-- figures the person states. The question names are copied from coa17-seat.l4 by script (work/gen_cases.py); the arguments
-- are positional, in the order of each question's inputs.

§ `Cases: the seat layer`


§§ `Cases: s 768`

-- A shareholder of an English company holds a certificate under the common seal that names her shares.
#ASSERT `Under section 768(1), is my share certificate prima facie evidence of my title to the shares` `England and Wales` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same certificate from a Scottish company: subsection (1) is limited to England and Wales and Northern Ireland, so not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 768(1), is my share certificate prima facie evidence of my title to the shares` Scotland TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Scottish company, certificate under the common seal, nobody has shown the contrary.
#ASSERT `Under section 768(2), is my share certificate from a Scottish company sufficient evidence of my title to the shares` Scotland TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The contrary has been shown: "unless the contrary is shown".
#ASSERT `Under section 768(2), is my share certificate from a Scottish company sufficient evidence of my title to the shares` Scotland TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An English company: subsection (2) is limited to Scotland.
#ASSERT `Under section 768(2), is my share certificate from a Scottish company sufficient evidence of my title to the shares` `England and Wales` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Cases: s 769`

-- Shares were allotted to me and no exception applies.
#ASSERT `Under section 769(1), must the company have my certificates or debentures ready for delivery after the allotment` `s 769(1) shares allotted` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The allotment was to a financial institution: subsection (2)(b) says subsection (1) does not apply.
#ASSERT `Under section 769(1), must the company have my certificates or debentures ready for delivery after the allotment` `s 769(1) shares allotted` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A share warrant has been issued, but the allotment was of debentures: (2)(c) speaks only of an allotment of shares.
#ASSERT `Under section 769(1), must the company have my certificates or debentures ready for delivery after the allotment` `s 769(1) debentures allotted` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Allotted 5 January 2026: two months after is 5 March 2026.
#ASSERT `Under section 769(1), by what day must the company have my certificates or debentures ready for delivery` (Date 5 1 2026) EQUALS Date 5 3 2026
-- Allotted 31 December 2025: the last day of February.
#ASSERT `Under section 769(1), by what day must the company have my certificates or debentures ready for delivery` (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
-- Nothing ready, and today is 6 March 2026, the day after the last day.
#ASSERT `Under section 769(3), is the company in default over my certificates or debentures` `s 769(1) shares allotted` (Date 5 1 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 6 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Ready on 5 March, the last day: in time.
#ASSERT `Under section 769(3), is the company in default over my certificates or debentures` `s 769(1) shares allotted` (Date 5 1 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 5 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not ready yet but the two months have not ended.
#ASSERT `Under section 769(3), is the company in default over my certificates or debentures` `s 769(1) shares allotted` (Date 5 1 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 5 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I am the director in default of a company that is in default.
#ASSERT `Under section 769(3), do I commit an offence as an officer of the company over a default on the certificates or debentures` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I am not an officer in default (section 1121): no offence by me.
#ASSERT `Under section 769(3), do I commit an offence as an officer of the company over a default on the certificates or debentures` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- If level 3 stands for 1000 pounds (an illustrative figure the person states: the Act does not give it).
#ASSERT `Under section 769(4), what is the most the company's officer can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` 1000 EQUALS JUST 1000

§§ `Cases: s 770`

-- No instrument delivered, not exempt, not under the Chapter 2 regulations: the company may not register.
#ASSERT `Under section 770(1), is the company barred from registering my transfer` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A proper instrument of transfer has been delivered: the bar is lifted.
#ASSERT `Under section 770(1), is the company barred from registering my transfer` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The right passed to me on a death by operation of law.
