#ASSERT `Under section 770(2), does section 770(1) leave unaffected the company's power to register me as shareholder or debenture holder where the right passed to me by operation of law` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No transmission by operation of law: not covered by subsection (2).
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 770(2), may the company still register me as shareholder or debenture holder where the right passed to me by operation of law` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING; the question asked whether the company may register, but the function answers whether subsection (1) leaves the company's power unaffected (the text of s 770(2) is "does not affect any power"); the facts and the expected values are unchanged
#ASSERT `Under section 770(2), does section 770(1) leave unaffected the company's power to register me as shareholder or debenture holder where the right passed to me by operation of law` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Cases: s 771`

-- My transfer of shares was lodged; no warrant, no transmission.
#ASSERT `Under section 771(1), must the company register my transfer or give me notice of refusal with its reasons` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A share warrant has been issued for the shares: subsection (5)(a) says this section does not apply.
#ASSERT `Under section 771(1), must the company register my transfer or give me notice of refusal with its reasons` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Lodged 5 January 2026: two months after is 5 March 2026.
#ASSERT `Under section 771(1), by what day must the company register my transfer or give me notice of refusal` (Date 5 1 2026) EQUALS Date 5 3 2026
-- Registered on 20 January, promptly.
#ASSERT `Under section 771(1), has the company complied with its duty on my lodged transfer` FALSE FALSE (Date 5 1 2026) `s 771(1)(a) registered the transfer` (Date 20 1 2026) TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Registered on 6 March: after the last day.
#ASSERT `Under section 771(1), has the company complied with its duty on my lodged transfer` FALSE FALSE (Date 5 1 2026) `s 771(1)(a) registered the transfer` (Date 6 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Nothing done yet on the last day: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Under section 771(1), has the company complied with its duty on my lodged transfer` FALSE FALSE (Date 5 1 2026) `s 771(1) did neither` (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 5 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The company does not yet have the transferee information: barred from registering.
#ASSERT `Under section 771(1A), is the company barred from registering my transfer until it has the information for its register of members` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The company refused; I reasonably ask for further information about its reasons.
#ASSERT `Under section 771(2), must the company give me further information about its reasons for refusing to register my transfer` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I ask for copies of the directors' minutes: "This does not include copies of minutes of meetings of directors."
#ASSERT `Under section 771(2), must the company give me further information about its reasons for refusing to register my transfer` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- My request is not one I may reasonably make: limited by its own wording, so not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 771(2), must the company give me further information about its reasons for refusing to register my transfer` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The company failed to comply and I am an officer in default.
#ASSERT `Under section 771(3), do I commit an offence as an officer of the company that fails to deal with a lodged transfer` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

