-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part coa18 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa18-cases-seat.l4: cases for the seat layer coa18-seat.l4 (Companies Act 2006, Parts 22 to 24, ss 791 to 859).
-- Each case states the facts a director, secretary, member or person dealing with a company would state, and the answer the
-- Act gives on them. Every expected value is written from the text, beside its assertion, before the run; a failing assertion
-- is a finding. Generated by work/gentests.py from work/tests/cases-seat.py (the layout only; the values are hand-written).
-- Every question of the seat layer has at least one case. The seat has one seat (the individual); there are no mirror cases.

§§ `Part 22: a notice requiring information about interests in shares (ss 791 to 796)`

-- A shareholder of a public company: Part 22 applies.
#ASSERT `Under section 791, does Part 22 apply to this company?` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A shareholder of a private company: "This Part applies only to public companies."
#ASSERT `Under section 791, does Part 22 apply to this company?` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A public company that knows I hold an interest may serve the notice.
#ASSERT `Under section 793(1), may the company give me a notice requiring information about my interest in its shares?` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A public company with no knowledge or belief about me: the Act does not say it may.
#ASSERT `Under section 793(1), may the company give me a notice requiring information about my interest in its shares?` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A private company: Part 22 does not apply, so there is no such power.
#ASSERT `Under section 793(1), may the company give me a notice requiring information about my interest in its shares?` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I sold my interest on 20 March 2024; the notice is dated 15 June 2026: within the three years (from 15 June 2023).
#ASSERT `Under section 793(1)(b), was my interest within the three years before the notice?` (Date 20 3 2024) (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- My interest ended on 1 January 2022: before the three years.
#ASSERT `Under section 793(1)(b), was my interest within the three years before the notice?` (Date 1 1 2022) (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I held an interest within the three years.
#ASSERT `Under section 793(2)(b), may the notice require me to give further information about my interest?` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 793(2)(b), may the notice require me to give further information about my interest?` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the seat question calls a function named for a power (the notice may require) that answered JUST FALSE because an if gate failed; the name-test sweep makes the function NOTHING (fork F42), so the question answers null; facts unchanged
-- I held none: "if he holds, or has ... held, any such interest".
#ASSERT `Under section 793(2)(b), may the notice require me to give further information about my interest?` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- My interest is current and another person also has one now.
#ASSERT `Under section 793(4), may the notice require me to give particulars of another interest in the shares?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- There is no other interest: "where" neither limb holds.
#ASSERT `Under section 793(4), may the notice require me to give particulars of another interest in the shares?` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I answered on the last day the notice allowed.
#ASSERT `Under section 793(7), did I give the information within the time the notice specified?` TRUE (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I answered a day late.
#ASSERT `Under section 793(7), did I give the information within the time the notice specified?` TRUE (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The time the notice allowed was not reasonable: the Act says "such reasonable time", so it does not answer.
#ASSERT `Under section 793(7), did I give the information within the time the notice specified?` FALSE (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A notice was served and the information was not given in time.
#ASSERT `Under section 794(1), may the company apply to the court for an order restricting my shares?` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The information was given: no application.
#ASSERT `Under section 794(1), may the company apply to the court for an order restricting my shares?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I did not comply and have no defence.
#ASSERT `Under section 795(1)(a), do I commit an offence by failing to comply with the notice?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I did not comply but can prove the requirement was frivolous or vexatious: s 795(2).
#ASSERT `Under section 795(1)(a), do I commit an offence by failing to comply with the notice?` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I complied: this subsection does not say I commit an offence; it does not answer.
#ASSERT `Under section 795(1)(a), do I commit an offence by failing to comply with the notice?` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- I knowingly gave a false answer.
#ASSERT `Under section 795(1)(b), do I commit an offence by a false statement in purported compliance with the notice?` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- My answer was wrong but neither knowing nor reckless: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 795(1)(b), do I commit an offence by a false statement in purported compliance with the notice?` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- On indictment: two years.
#ASSERT `Under section 795(3), what is the longest prison term, in months, on conviction?` `on conviction on indictment` EQUALS JUST 24
-- Summary conviction in England and Wales: twelve months.
#ASSERT `Under section 795(3), what is the longest prison term, in months, on conviction?` `on summary conviction in England and Wales` EQUALS JUST 12
-- Summary conviction in Scotland: six months.
#ASSERT `Under section 795(3), what is the longest prison term, in months, on conviction?` `on summary conviction in Scotland` EQUALS JUST 6
-- Summary conviction in Northern Ireland: six months.
#ASSERT `Under section 795(3), what is the longest prison term, in months, on conviction?` `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` EQUALS JUST 6
-- Summary conviction without saying where: the Act divides it by place; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 795(3), what is the longest prison term, in months, on conviction?` `on summary conviction` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Secretary of State has exempted me for the time being.
#ASSERT `Under section 796(1), am I not obliged to comply with a notice under section 793?` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No exemption: this subsection does not say I am obliged either.
#ASSERT `Under section 796(1), am I not obliged to comply with a notice under section 793?` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Part 22: orders restricting shares and the court (ss 797 to 802)`

-- My shares are under an order and no direction covers the transfer.
#ASSERT `Under section 797(1)(a), is a transfer of my shares void?` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- My shares are not under an order: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 797(1)(a), is a transfer of my shares void?` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The court directed that the transfer is not a breach: s 797(4)(a).
#ASSERT `Under section 797(1)(a), is a transfer of my shares void?` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Under an order: no voting rights are exercisable.
#ASSERT `Under section 797(1)(b), are no voting rights exercisable in respect of my shares?` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Under an order, outside a liquidation: no payment may be made.
#ASSERT `Under section 797(1)(d), is no payment to be made of sums due from the company on my shares?` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The payment is made in a liquidation: "except in a liquidation".
#ASSERT `Under section 797(1)(d), is no payment to be made of sums due from the company on my shares?` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I sold shares knowing they were restricted.
#ASSERT `Under section 798(2)(a), do I commit an offence by disposing of shares subject to restrictions?` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I did not know they were restricted: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 798(2)(a), do I commit an offence by disposing of shares subject to restrictions?` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- I voted the shares knowing they were restricted.
#ASSERT `Under section 798(2)(b), do I commit an offence by voting shares subject to restrictions?` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A court direction covers the act: s 798(5).
#ASSERT `Under section 798(2)(b), do I commit an offence by voting shares subject to restrictions?` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I am a person aggrieved by the order.
#ASSERT `Under section 799(2), may I apply to the court to relax the restrictions on shares?` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither the company nor aggrieved: "may be made by" does not say "only".
#ASSERT `Under section 799(2), may I apply to the court to relax the restrictions on shares?` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Facts disclosed and no unfair advantage: the bar does not apply.
#ASSERT `Under section 800(3), is the court barred from ordering that the shares cease to be subject to restrictions?` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Transfer for valuable consideration but the court has not approved it: barred.
#ASSERT `Under section 800(3), is the court barred from ordering that the shares cease to be subject to restrictions?` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I am the only person beneficially interested: the whole proceeds with interest.
#ASSERT `Under section 802(3), how much of the proceeds of sale must the court order paid to me?` 1000 50 FALSE 1 4 EQUALS JUST 1050
-- Another person was interested: a quarter of 1050.
#ASSERT `Under section 802(3), how much of the proceeds of sale must the court order paid to me?` 1000 50 TRUE 1 4 EQUALS JUST 262.5

§§ `Part 22: members requiring the company to investigate, and the report (ss 803 to 807)`

-- Members holding exactly 10% of the voting paid-up capital have asked.
#ASSERT `Under section 803(2), is the company required to investigate interests in its shares?` TRUE 100 1000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Members holding 9.9% have asked: not enough.
#ASSERT `Under section 803(2), is the company required to investigate interests in its shares?` TRUE 99 1000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A signed paper request stating what it must.
