-- The investigation concluded within three months: none.
#ASSERT `Under section 805(2), how many interim reports must the company prepare?` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 20 2 2026) EQUALS 0
-- Two three-month periods ended before the conclusion: two.
#ASSERT `Under section 805(2), how many interim reports must the company prepare?` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 2 7 2026) EQUALS 2
-- Report available on Friday 2 January; 6 January listed: Monday 5, Wednesday 7, Thursday 8.
#ASSERT `Under section 805(6), by what date must the company notify the members where the report is available?` (Date 2 1 2026) (LIST (Date 6 1 2026)) EQUALS (Date 8 1 2026)
-- With no days off: Monday 5, Tuesday 6, Wednesday 7.
#ASSERT `Under section 805(6), by what date must the company notify the members where the report is available?` (Date 2 1 2026) EMPTY EQUALS (Date 7 1 2026)
-- In default for 14 days.
#ASSERT `Under section 806(1), does the company commit an offence by failing to notify the registrar of the place of the reports?` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not yet 14 days.
#ASSERT `Under section 806(1), does the company commit an offence by failing to notify the registrar of the place of the reports?` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I am an officer in default.
#ASSERT `Under section 806(1)(b), do I as an officer commit an offence?` TRUE ((JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I do not know whether I am "in default" (s 1121): not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 806(1)(b), do I as an officer commit an offence?` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- The company is not in default for 14 days.
#ASSERT `Under section 806(1)(b), do I as an officer commit an offence?` FALSE ((JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 807(1), must the report be open to my inspection without charge?` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE; retitled because the function states a duty on the report ("must be open to inspection by any person"), not my privilege to inspect; facts and expected value unchanged.
-- A report prepared under s 805: open to any person without charge.
#ASSERT `Under section 807(1), must a report the company prepared on its investigation be open to inspection by any person without charge?` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I asked and paid the prescribed fee.
#ASSERT `Under section 807(2), am I entitled to a copy of the report?` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I have not paid the fee.
#ASSERT `Under section 807(2), am I entitled to a copy of the report?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Request received Monday 5 January; 6 January not a working day: ten working days end on Tuesday 20 January.
#ASSERT `Under section 807(2), by what date must the company provide the copy?` (Date 5 1 2026) (LIST (Date 6 1 2026)) EQUALS (Date 20 1 2026)
-- With no days off: Monday 19 January.
#ASSERT `Under section 807(2), by what date must the company provide the copy?` (Date 5 1 2026) EMPTY EQUALS (Date 19 1 2026)

