-- It does not state the number of those shares.
#ASSERT `Under section 825(4), does my notification contain what is required?` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 23: distributions (ss 829 to 849)`

-- A cash dividend to members.
#ASSERT `Under section 829(1), is this a distribution?` `s 829(1) another description of distribution of the company's assets to its members, whether in cash or otherwise` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A bonus issue: not a distribution.
#ASSERT `Under section 829(1), is this a distribution?` `s 829(2)(a) an issue of shares as fully or partly paid bonus shares` NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A redemption out of capital in accordance with Part 18: not a distribution.
#ASSERT `Under section 829(1), is this a distribution?` `s 829(2)(c) the redemption or purchase of any of the company's own shares out of capital (including the proceeds of any fresh issue of shares) or out of unrealised profits` ((JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Realised profits 1000 of which 200 used; realised losses 300 of which 100 written off: 800 less 200.
#ASSERT `Under section 830(2), what are the company's profits available for distribution?` 1000 200 300 100 EQUALS 600
-- A dividend of exactly the profits available.
#ASSERT `Under section 830(1), is the distribution within the profits available for the purpose?` 600 600 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A dividend of one pound more.
#ASSERT `Under section 830(1), is the distribution within the profits available for the purpose?` 601 600 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Net assets 1000 against 800; a distribution of 200 leaves exactly 800.
#ASSERT `Under section 831(1), is the distribution within the net asset restriction on public companies?` TRUE 1000 600 200 200 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- One pound more would take net assets below 800.
#ASSERT `Under section 831(1), is the distribution within the net asset restriction on public companies?` TRUE 1000 600 200 201 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A private company is not mentioned by s 831(1).
#ASSERT `Under section 831(1), is the distribution within the net asset restriction on public companies?` FALSE 1000 600 200 201 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Share premium 100, capital redemption reserve 50, unrealised excess 270, other reserves 15.
#ASSERT `Under section 831(4), what are the company's undistributable reserves?` 100 50 500 200 50 100 20 10 5 EQUALS 435
-- Assets 1800 less 300 is 1500: exactly one and a half times 1000.
#ASSERT `Under section 832(3), does the distribution leave the investment company with enough assets?` 1800 1000 300 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- One pound more leaves less than one and a half times.
#ASSERT `Under section 832(3), does the distribution leave the investment company with enough assets?` 1800 1000 301 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The last annual accounts would show a contravention.
#ASSERT `Under section 836(2)(a), may the company justify the distribution by reference to interim accounts?` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- They would not: "where".
#ASSERT `Under section 836(2)(a), may the company justify the distribution by reference to interim accounts?` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- During the first accounting reference period.
#ASSERT `Under section 836(2)(b), may the company justify the distribution by reference to initial accounts?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither condition.
#ASSERT `Under section 836(2)(b), may the company justify the distribution by reference to initial accounts?` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Proposed 1000 plus earlier distributions 400 plus relevant payments 100.
#ASSERT `Under section 840(1), what amount counts as the proposed distribution?` 1000 400 100 EQUALS 1500
-- Sold to a member for 500, book value 400: zero.
#ASSERT `Under section 845(2), what is the amount of the distribution in kind?` 500 400 EQUALS 0
-- Sold to a member for 300, book value 400: 100.
#ASSERT `Under section 845(2), what is the amount of the distribution in kind?` 300 400 EQUALS 100
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 847(2), must I repay the distribution?` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 847(2)(a) liable to repay the distribution or that part of it to the company`; retitled because the function answers what the member is liable to do (repay, pay the value, or not liable), not whether the member must repay; facts and expected value unchanged.
-- A cash dividend I knew was unlawful: repay it.
#ASSERT `Under section 847(2), what am I liable to do about the distribution I received?` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 847(2)(a) liable to repay the distribution or that part of it to the company`
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 847(2), must I repay the distribution?` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 847(2)(b) liable to pay the company a sum equal to the value of the distribution or that part at that time`; retitled because the function answers what the member is liable to do (repay, pay the value, or not liable), not whether the member must repay; facts and expected value unchanged.
-- A distribution in kind I knew was unlawful: pay its value.
#ASSERT `Under section 847(2), what am I liable to do about the distribution I received?` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 847(2)(b) liable to pay the company a sum equal to the value of the distribution or that part at that time`
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 847(2), must I repay the distribution?` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 847(2) not liable under this subsection`; retitled because the function answers what the member is liable to do (repay, pay the value, or not liable), not whether the member must repay; facts and expected value unchanged.
-- I neither knew nor had reasonable grounds to believe: not liable under s 847(2).
#ASSERT `Under section 847(2), what am I liable to do about the distribution I received?` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 847(2) not liable under this subsection`
-- An unrealised profit: the company must not.
#ASSERT `Under section 849, may the company apply the profit in paying up debentures or unpaid amounts on its shares?` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Intended for continuing use in the company's activities.
#ASSERT `Under section 853(6), is the asset a fixed asset?` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not so intended: "means".
#ASSERT `Under section 853(6), is the asset a fixed asset?` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 24: the confirmation statement (ss 853A to 853L)`

-- A review period beginning 1 March 2025 ends on 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `Under section 853A(5), on what day does the review period end?` (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS (Date 28 2 2026)
-- Incorporated on a leap day: the anniversary is taken as 1 March, so it ends on 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `Under section 853A(5), on what day does the review period end?` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS (Date 28 2 2025)
-- Fourteen days after the review period ends on 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `Under section 853A(1), by what day must the company deliver its confirmation statement?` (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS (Date 14 3 2026)
-- The company filed early with a confirmation date of 31 December 2025.
#ASSERT `Under section 853A(6), on what day does the next review period begin?` (Date 28 2 2026) (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS (Date 1 1 2026)
-- The company changed its principal business during the period.
#ASSERT `Under section 853C(2), must the company notify the registrar of a change in its principal business activities?` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No change.
#ASSERT `Under section 853C(2), must the company notify the registrar of a change in its principal business activities?` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- First statement: the activities had changed by the time of incorporation.
#ASSERT `Under section 853C(2), must the company notify the registrar of a change in its principal business activities?` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A company with share capital whose capital has changed.
#ASSERT `Under section 853D(2), must the company deliver a statement of capital with its confirmation statement?` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Nothing has changed since the last statement of capital.
#ASSERT `Under section 853D(2), must the company deliver a statement of capital with its confirmation statement?` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I hold exactly 5% of the class.
#ASSERT `Under section 853G(6)(a), must my name and address be delivered as a holder of 5% or more of a class?` 50 1000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I hold 4.9%: not mentioned.
#ASSERT `Under section 853G(6)(a), must my name and address be delivered as a holder of 5% or more of a class?` 49 1000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not delivered, and today is the fifteenth day after the review period.
#ASSERT `Under section 853L(1)(a), has the company committed an offence by not delivering its confirmation statement in time?` (Date 28 2 2026) NOTHING (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Delivered on the fourteenth day: in time.
#ASSERT `Under section 853L(1)(a), has the company committed an offence by not delivering its confirmation statement in time?` (Date 28 2 2026) (JUST (Date 14 3 2026)) (Date 20 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not yet delivered but the 14 days have not ended.
#ASSERT `Under section 853L(1)(a), has the company committed an offence by not delivering its confirmation statement in time?` (Date 28 2 2026) NOTHING (Date 14 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Late, and I am an officer in default.
#ASSERT `Under section 853L(1)(b), have I as an officer committed an offence by the company's late confirmation statement?` (Date 28 2 2026) NOTHING (Date 15 3 2026) ((JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Late, but I do not know whether I am "in default": not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 853L(1)(b), have I as an officer committed an offence by the company's late confirmation statement?` (Date 28 2 2026) NOTHING (Date 15 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- England and Wales: the greater of 500 and one-tenth of level 4 (2500): 500.
#ASSERT `Under section 853L(6), what is the most the daily default fine can be in pounds?` `on summary conviction in England and Wales` 2500 EQUALS JUST 500
-- England and Wales with level 4 at 10000: one-tenth is 1000.
#ASSERT `Under section 853L(6), what is the most the daily default fine can be in pounds?` `on summary conviction in England and Wales` 10000 EQUALS JUST 1000
-- Scotland: one-tenth of level 5 (5000).
#ASSERT `Under section 853L(6), what is the most the daily default fine can be in pounds?` `on summary conviction in Scotland` 5000 EQUALS JUST 500
-- Summary conviction without a place: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 853L(6), what is the most the daily default fine can be in pounds?` `on summary conviction` 5000 EQUALS NOTHING

-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part coa19 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa19-cases-seat.l4: cases for coa19-seat.l4: every question of the seat is asked at least once, on the facts a person in the seat would state, and the answer is written from the text
-- of the section named in the comment above each assertion, never from the code's output. The assertion lines are generated by work/gen-cases.py from the seat's own parameter lists
-- (so a parameter name cannot be mistyped); the facts and the expected answers are the table written by hand in that script. Dates are illustrative; the pounds a level on the standard
-- scale or the statutory maximum stands for, and the prescribed fee, are not in the Act: the figures 1,000, 5,000 and 5 below are supplied by the cases, not taken from the Act.

§ `Cases: the questions of the individual (ss 859A to 894)`

-- s 859A(1), (6): a UK-registered company creates an ordinary charge: the section applies
#ASSERT (`Under section 859A(1) and (6), does the registration requirement of section 859A apply to a charge my company creates` WITH `my company is registered in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland` IS TRUE, `my company creates a charge` IS TRUE, `the charge is a landlord's charge on a cash deposit given as security for a lease of land` IS FALSE, `the charge is a Lloyd's member's charge for its underwriting business` IS FALSE, `the charge is excluded by another Act` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 859A(1), (6): the company is not UK-registered: "applies where a company creates a charge"
#ASSERT (`Under section 859A(1) and (6), does the registration requirement of section 859A apply to a charge my company creates` WITH `my company is registered in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland` IS FALSE, `my company creates a charge` IS TRUE, `the charge is a landlord's charge on a cash deposit given as security for a lease of land` IS FALSE, `the charge is a Lloyd's member's charge for its underwriting business` IS FALSE, `the charge is excluded by another Act` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 859A(1), (6): no charge is created
#ASSERT (`Under section 859A(1) and (6), does the registration requirement of section 859A apply to a charge my company creates` WITH `my company is registered in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland` IS TRUE, `my company creates a charge` IS FALSE, `the charge is a landlord's charge on a cash deposit given as security for a lease of land` IS FALSE, `the charge is a Lloyd's member's charge for its underwriting business` IS FALSE, `the charge is excluded by another Act` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 859A(1), (6): (6)(a) a landlord's charge on a cash deposit is excluded
#ASSERT (`Under section 859A(1) and (6), does the registration requirement of section 859A apply to a charge my company creates` WITH `my company is registered in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland` IS TRUE, `my company creates a charge` IS TRUE, `the charge is a landlord's charge on a cash deposit given as security for a lease of land` IS TRUE, `the charge is a Lloyd's member's charge for its underwriting business` IS FALSE, `the charge is excluded by another Act` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 859A(1), (6): (6)(b) a Lloyd's member's underwriting charge is excluded
