-- s 859C(2): a charge on acquired property, a statement delivered (no time limit in (2))
#ASSERT (`Under section 859C(1) to (3), must the registrar register a charge that already exists on property my company has acquired` WITH `my company is registered in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland` IS TRUE, `my company has acquired property or an undertaking` IS TRUE, `it is subject to a charge` IS TRUE, `the charge is a landlord's charge on a cash deposit given as security for a lease of land` IS FALSE, `the charge is a Lloyd's member's charge for its underwriting business` IS FALSE, `the charge is excluded by another Act` IS FALSE, `the company or a person interested in the charge delivered a statement of particulars to the registrar for registration` IS TRUE, `my statement contains every particular section 859D requires` IS TRUE, `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument` IS FALSE, `a certified copy of the instrument was delivered with the statement` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
