-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part coa21 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa21-cases-seat.l4: cases for the seat layer coa21-seat.l4 (the questions of an individual who is a director, company secretary or member of
-- a company, or who deals with one, in ss 942 to 993). Each case is a person with facts; the expected answer is written from the text of the section
-- named in the case's comment, before the run, and never copied from the code's output.
-- Reading an answer: JUST TRUE is yes; JUST FALSE is the text's own no; NOTHING is "the text does not answer this on these facts".

§ `Cases for the seat layer`

§§ `Chapter 1: the Takeover Panel`

-- Case: Ben, a director, is accused of breaching a Panel rule whose text was not yet public when he acted (s 944(4): protected if he shows that).
#ASSERT `Under section 944(4), am I protected from being taken to have contravened a Takeover Panel rule because its text had not been made available to the public` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 944(4), am I protected from being taken to have contravened a Takeover Panel rule because its text had not been made available to the public` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Case: a member who wants to rely on the instrument in legal proceedings may require a certified copy (s 944(7)).
#ASSERT `Under section 944(7), may I require the Takeover Panel to certify a copy of its rules instrument for use in legal proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 944(7), may I require the Takeover Panel to certify a copy of its rules instrument for use in legal proceedings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Case: the Panel's rules say such a ruling binds, and no review or appeal is pending (s 945(2)).
#ASSERT `Under section 945(2), is a Takeover Panel ruling binding on me` `Under sections 942 to 993 it is so` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 945(2), is a Takeover Panel ruling binding on me` `Under sections 942 to 993 it is so` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 945(2), is a Takeover Panel ruling binding on me` `Under sections 942 to 993 I do not know` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Case: Chen received a written, specific notice for what the Panel reasonably needs; no privilege (s 947(1), (3), (10)).
#ASSERT `Under section 947, must I produce the documents or give the information the Takeover Panel has required by notice` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Case: the same, but he could maintain legal professional privilege (s 947(10): not required).
#ASSERT `Under section 947, must I produce the documents or give the information the Takeover Panel has required by notice` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Case: not reasonably required in connection with the Panel's functions (s 947(3): applies only to what is).
#ASSERT `Under section 947, must I produce the documents or give the information the Takeover Panel has required by notice` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Case: no notice in writing: the power is by notice in writing, and the text says nothing about the case.
#ASSERT `Under section 947, must I produce the documents or give the information the Takeover Panel has required by notice` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
