#ASSERT `Under section 949(1), am I guilty of the offence of disclosing information in contravention of section 948` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Case: he did not know, and had no reason to suspect, that the information had been given to the Panel (s 949(1)(a)).
#ASSERT `Under section 949(1), am I guilty of the offence of disclosing information in contravention of section 948` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Case: he took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence (s 949(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `Under section 949(1), am I guilty of the offence of disclosing information in contravention of section 948` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Case: the disclosure is not in contravention of section 948 (it helps the Panel): the offence is of a person who discloses in contravention of section 948.
#ASSERT `Under section 949(1), am I guilty of the offence of disclosing information in contravention of section 948` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Case: on indictment, two years or a fine (or both) (s 949(2)(a)).
#ASSERT `Under section 949(2), what penalty may I face if I am convicted of disclosing information in contravention of section 948` `on conviction on indictment` EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, JUST (Period OF 2, Years), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE)
-- Case: summary conviction in Scotland: six months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (s 949(2)(b)(ii)).
#ASSERT `Under section 949(2), what penalty may I face if I am convicted of disclosing information in contravention of section 948` `on summary conviction in Scotland` EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
