#ASSERT `Under section 984(2), by what day must I exercise my right to require the offeror to buy my shares` (Date 30 6 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS Date 30 9 2027
-- Case: one month from 31 January 2027 (s 984(3)).
#ASSERT `Under section 984(3), by what day must the offeror give me notice of my right to be bought out` (Date 31 1 2027) EQUALS Date 28 2 2027
-- Case: the last of the six weeks (s 986(2)).
#ASSERT `Under section 986(2), am I still in time to apply to the court against the squeeze-out notice I was given` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 12 4 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 986(2), am I still in time to apply to the court against the squeeze-out notice I was given` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 13 4 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Case: the person is the offeror's nominee (s 988(1)(a)).
#ASSERT `Under section 988, is this person an associate of the offeror` TRUE `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` FALSE FALSE 0 0 `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Case: the offeror controls one-third of the person's voting power (s 988(1)(c), (3)(b)).
#ASSERT `Under section 988, is this person an associate of the offeror` FALSE `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` FALSE FALSE 100 300 `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Case: just under one-third, and no other link (s 988(1): the list is the whole of the definition).
#ASSERT `Under section 988, is this person an associate of the offeror` FALSE `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` FALSE FALSE 99 300 `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Case: the offeror is an individual and the person is his spouse (s 988(1)(e)).
#ASSERT `Under section 988, is this person an associate of the offeror` FALSE `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` FALSE FALSE 0 0 `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Case: the offeror is a company, so paragraph (e) does not reach the person.
#ASSERT `Under section 988, is this person an associate of the offeror` FALSE `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` FALSE FALSE 0 0 `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Case: it is not known whether the person is a group company of the offeror (section 1159).
#ASSERT `Under section 988, is this person an associate of the offeror` FALSE `Under sections 942 to 993 I do not know` FALSE FALSE 0 0 `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Case: a listed company's debentures carrying voting rights are treated as shares (s 990(1)).
#ASSERT `Under section 990(1), are my company's debentures treated as shares for the purposes of Chapter 3` `Under sections 942 to 993 it is so` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 990(1), are my company's debentures treated as shares for the purposes of Chapter 3` `Under sections 942 to 993 it is so` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 990(1), are my company's debentures treated as shares for the purposes of Chapter 3` `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Case: a listed company's report must describe the structure of its capital (Schedule 7 para 13(2)(a) as inserted).
#ASSERT `Under section 992(2), must the directors' report of my company contain detailed information on this matter` (Date 1 1 2007) `Under sections 942 to 993 it is so` `s 992(2) para 13(2)(a) the structure of the company's capital` FALSE FALSE `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Case: a change-of-control agreement whose disclosure would be seriously prejudicial and which need not otherwise be disclosed (para 13(5)).
#ASSERT `Under section 992(2), must the directors' report of my company contain detailed information on this matter` (Date 1 1 2007) `Under sections 942 to 993 it is so` `s 992(2) para 13(2)(j) any significant agreements that take effect, alter or terminate upon a change of control following a takeover bid` FALSE FALSE `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Case: the company had no voting securities admitted to trading on a regulated market (para 13(1)).
#ASSERT `Under section 992(2), must the directors' report of my company contain detailed information on this matter` (Date 1 1 2007) `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` `s 992(2) para 13(2)(a) the structure of the company's capital` FALSE FALSE `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Case: a financial year beginning on 20 May 2006 (s 992(6)).
#ASSERT `Under section 992(6), do the section 992 amendments apply to my company's directors' report` (Date 20 5 2006) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 992(6), do the section 992 amendments apply to my company's directors' report` (Date 19 5 2006) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Case: a director who knowingly took part in carrying on the business with intent to defraud the company's creditors (s 993(1)).
#ASSERT `Under section 993(1), have I committed the offence of fraudulent trading` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Case: the business was not carried on with any fraudulent intent or purpose (s 993(1): if it is, every person who is knowingly a party commits an offence).
#ASSERT `Under section 993(1), have I committed the offence of fraudulent trading` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Case: fraudulent business, but the person was not knowingly a party.
#ASSERT `Under section 993(1), have I committed the offence of fraudulent trading` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Case: up to ten years or a fine (or both) on indictment (s 993(3)(a)).
#ASSERT `Under section 993(3), what penalty may I face if I am convicted of fraudulent trading` `on conviction on indictment` EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, JUST (Period OF 10, Years), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE)
-- Case: six months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum in Northern Ireland (s 993(3)(b)(ii)).
#ASSERT `Under section 993(3), what penalty may I face if I am convicted of fraudulent trading` `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)

-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part coa22 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa22-cases-seat.l4: cases for the seat layer (coa22-seat.l4), Companies Act 2006 ss 994-1043 (Parts 30 to 33).
-- Each case states the facts a person in the seat would state, in the order the question's inputs are declared, and the
-- answer expected from the text of the Act (not from running the code). T = JUST TRUE, F = JUST FALSE, NOTHING = the text
-- does not say ("not covered"). Pounds and dates are test figures, not the Act's. The questions whose answer is a date,
-- a name or a number have no NOTHING case: only the yes/no questions can be "not covered".
-- Both builds of the stable binary must agree on every line.

§ `Seat cases`

-- Under section 994(1), may I apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30 on the ground of unfair prejudice
-- a member of a company formed under the Act whose affairs are unfairly prejudicial to members generally
#ASSERT `Under section 994(1), may I apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30 on the ground of unfair prejudice` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a person to whom shares passed by operation of law is treated as a member
#ASSERT `Under section 994(1), may I apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30 on the ground of unfair prejudice` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a member, on the ground of an act or omission that is prejudicial
#ASSERT `Under section 994(1), may I apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30 on the ground of unfair prejudice` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not a member and no shares by operation of law: the text does not say such a person may not petition
#ASSERT `Under section 994(1), may I apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30 on the ground of unfair prejudice` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a member with no ground stated: the text does not decide
#ASSERT `Under section 994(1), may I apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30 on the ground of unfair prejudice` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 995(2), may the Secretary of State apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30 about my company
-- report received, body corporate liable to be wound up, it appears the affairs are unfairly prejudicial
#ASSERT `Under section 995(2), may the Secretary of State apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30 about my company` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- none of the four triggers in section 995(1) has happened: the text lists them without "only"
#ASSERT `Under section 995(2), may the Secretary of State apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30 about my company` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 996(2), may the court's order on a Part 30 petition contain a particular provision
-- the court is satisfied; the order may regulate the conduct of the company's affairs
#ASSERT `Under section 996(2), may the court's order on a Part 30 petition contain a particular provision` TRUE `s 996(2)(a) regulate the conduct of the company's affairs in the future` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the catch-all provision
#ASSERT `Under section 996(2), may the court's order on a Part 30 petition contain a particular provision` TRUE `s 996(2) any other provision for giving relief under subsection (1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 996(2), may the court's order on a Part 30 petition contain a particular provision` FALSE `s 996(2)(a) regulate the conduct of the company's affairs in the future` EQUALS JUST FALSE; name-test sweep of 2026-11-12: a grant named "may" whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING, not JUST FALSE (the other reading is JUST FALSE, fork F18); the facts are unchanged
-- the court is not satisfied that the petition is well founded: the text does not say its order may not contain the provision
#ASSERT `Under section 996(2), may the court's order on a Part 30 petition contain a particular provision` FALSE `s 996(2)(a) regulate the conduct of the company's affairs in the future` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 996(2)(e), where the order provides for the company itself to buy shares, does the order provide for the reduction of the company's capital accordingly
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 996(2)(e), where the order provides for the company itself to buy shares, must its capital be reduced accordingly` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE; question retitled to ask what the function answers (subject: the function answers whether the order provides for the reduction, not whether the capital must be reduced); facts and expected value unchanged
-- the order provides for the company to buy shares
#ASSERT `Under section 996(2)(e), where the order provides for the company itself to buy shares, does the order provide for the reduction of the company's capital accordingly` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 996(2)(e), where the order provides for the company itself to buy shares, must its capital be reduced accordingly` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING; question retitled to ask what the function answers (subject: the function answers whether the order provides for the reduction, not whether the capital must be reduced); facts and expected value unchanged
-- no purchase by the company itself: the text does not say
#ASSERT `Under section 996(2)(e), where the order provides for the company itself to buy shares, does the order provide for the reduction of the company's capital accordingly` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 998(1), must my company deliver a copy of the court's Part 30 order to the registrar
-- the order alters the constitution
#ASSERT `Under section 998(1), must my company deliver a copy of the court's Part 30 order to the registrar` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the order does not alter the constitution
#ASSERT `Under section 998(1), must my company deliver a copy of the court's Part 30 order to the registrar` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 998(2), what is the last day for my company to deliver a copy of the court's Part 30 order to the registrar
-- 14 days from the order
#ASSERT `Under section 998(2), what is the last day for my company to deliver a copy of the court's Part 30 order to the registrar` (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE 0 EQUALS Date 15 3 2026
-- the court allowed 28 days
