-- copy delivered on 10 March, in time
#ASSERT `Under section 998(3), have I, as an officer of the company, committed an offence by the company's default in delivering the copy of the order` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE 0 TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not yet 14 days: no default yet
#ASSERT `Under section 998(3), have I, as an officer of the company, committed an offence by the company's default in delivering the copy of the order` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE 0 FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the officer did nothing to cause the default: the text does not say he commits the offence
#ASSERT `Under section 998(3), have I, as an officer of the company, committed an offence by the company's default in delivering the copy of the order` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE 0 FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 998(4), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for an offence under section 998, in pounds
-- level 3 stands for 1,000 pounds (a test figure, not the Act's)
#ASSERT `Under section 998(4), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for an offence under section 998, in pounds` 1000 EQUALS JUST 1000

-- Under section 999(2)(a), must the copy of the order delivered to the registrar be accompanied by a copy of the company's articles as amended
-- the order alters the constitution and amends the articles
