#ASSERT `Under section 1032A(11), have I, as an officer or shadow director of the company restored by the court, committed an offence by its default` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no default
#ASSERT `Under section 1032A(11), have I, as an officer or shadow director of the company restored by the court, committed an offence by its default` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 1033(1), under what name is the company restored to the register
-- administrative restoration; the former name is available; no other name specified
#ASSERT `Under section 1033(1), under what name is the company restored to the register` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 1033(1) the name it had before it was dissolved or struck off the register`
-- the former name would contravene section 66, no other name specified
#ASSERT `Under section 1033(1), under what name is the company restored to the register` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 1033(2)(b) its registered number, as if its registered number was also its name`

-- Under section 1033(5)(a), what is the last day for my company, restored under its registered number, to change its name
-- 14 days after the restoration
#ASSERT `Under section 1033(5)(a), what is the last day for my company, restored under its registered number, to change its name` (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS Date 15 6 2026

-- Under section 1033(6), have I, as an officer of the company, committed an offence by its failure to change its name or give notice
-- the company failed; I am an officer who permitted it
#ASSERT `Under section 1033(6), have I, as an officer of the company, committed an offence by its failure to change its name or give notice` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the company did not fail
#ASSERT `Under section 1033(6), have I, as an officer of the company, committed an offence by its failure to change its name or give notice` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the officer is not shown to be in default: the text does not say
#ASSERT `Under section 1033(6), have I, as an officer of the company, committed an offence by its failure to change its name or give notice` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 1034(1), may I dispose of property that vested in me as bona vacantia, despite the company's possible restoration
-- property vested in me by section 1012
#ASSERT `Under section 1034(1), may I dispose of property that vested in me as bona vacantia, despite the company's possible restoration` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not so vested: the text does not say
#ASSERT `Under section 1034(1), may I dispose of property that vested in me as bona vacantia, despite the company's possible restoration` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 1034(2)(b), what must the Crown or the Duke of Cornwall pay the restored company for property it disposed of, in pounds
-- restored; money received: the amount
#ASSERT `Under section 1034(2)(b), what must the Crown or the Duke of Cornwall pay the restored company for property it disposed of, in pounds` TRUE TRUE TRUE 5000 0 0 EQUALS JUST 5000
-- restored; no consideration: the value of the property
#ASSERT `Under section 1034(2)(b), what must the Crown or the Duke of Cornwall pay the restored company for property it disposed of, in pounds` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 0 8000 EQUALS JUST 8000

-- Under section 1034(3), what is the least the Crown or the Duke of Cornwall must pay after deducting the Crown representative's reasonable costs, in pounds
-- amount 5000, costs 1200 of which 200 already paid: 1000 may be deducted, so at least 4000 is payable
#ASSERT `Under section 1034(3), what is the least the Crown or the Duke of Cornwall must pay after deducting the Crown representative's reasonable costs, in pounds` 5000 1200 200 EQUALS JUST 4000

