-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part coa24 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa24-cases-seat.l4: one or more cases for every question of the seat layer (coa24-seat.l4), put in the words of the person in the seat.
-- Each expected answer was decided from the text of the section before the run; none was copied from the encoding's output.
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE are the Act's answers; NOTHING means the Act does not decide the case. The pounds in the fine cases
-- are figures supplied by the caller (1,000 for level 5, and so on): the Act does not state them and they stand for nothing.

-- Maria, a director, told the registrar something because s 1092A required it, and is charged with an offence outside the list: protected.
#ASSERT `Under section 1092C(1), is a statement I made in response to the registrar's requirement protected from use against me in criminal proceedings` TRUE `s 1092C(2) any other offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Charged instead with a false-statement offence under s 1112: subsection (1) does not apply, and the Act does not say the statement may be used: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 1092C(1), is a statement I made in response to the registrar's requirement protected from use against me in criminal proceedings` TRUE `s 1092C(2)(a)(i) an offence under section 1112 or 1112A` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The statement was volunteered, not made in response to a requirement: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 1092C(1), is a statement I made in response to the registrar's requirement protected from use against me in criminal proceedings` FALSE `s 1092C(2) any other offence` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A notice issued on 10 February 2026: the 14 days beginning that day end on 23 February 2026.
#ASSERT `Under section 1093(1)(b), by what date must my company resolve the inconsistency the registrar has told it about` (Date 10 2 2026) EQUALS (Date 23 2 2026)
-- The notice (issued 10 Feb 2026, dated) was answered on 24 February 2026, one day after the period ended: an offence by the company.
#ASSERT `Under section 1093(3), has my company committed an offence by not resolving the inconsistency in time` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 2 2026) TRUE (Date 24 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Answered on 23 February 2026, the last day: no offence.
#ASSERT `Under section 1093(3), has my company committed an offence by not resolving the inconsistency in time` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 2 2026) TRUE (Date 23 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not answered, asked on 20 February 2026 while the period still runs: no offence yet.
#ASSERT `Under section 1093(3), has my company committed an offence by not resolving the inconsistency in time` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 2 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 20 2 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not answered, asked on 1 March 2026: an offence.
#ASSERT `Under section 1093(3), has my company committed an offence by not resolving the inconsistency in time` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 2 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No notice under s 1093(1) was given: the offence of subsection (3) is not in play.
#ASSERT `Under section 1093(3), has my company committed an offence by not resolving the inconsistency in time` FALSE TRUE (Date 10 2 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A director who authorised the failure, notice not answered by 1 March 2026: guilty.
#ASSERT `Under section 1093(3)(b), have I committed an offence as an officer of my company that did not resolve the inconsistency in time` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 2 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 3 2026) `s 1121(2)(a) a director` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A director who did nothing wrong: not in default.
#ASSERT `Under section 1093(3)(b), have I committed an offence as an officer of my company that did not resolve the inconsistency in time` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 2 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 3 2026) `s 1121(2)(a) a director` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Someone outside the s 1121(2) positions who permitted it: the list "includes", so not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 1093(3)(b), have I committed an offence as an officer of my company that did not resolve the inconsistency in time` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 2 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 3 2026) `s 1121(2) none of these positions` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- First conviction: level 5 (the caller supplies 1,000 as the amount of level 5).
#ASSERT `Under section 1093(4), what is the most I can be fined for the offence of not resolving the inconsistency` `s 1093(4) the text read as one-tenth of level 5` FALSE 0 400 1000 EQUALS JUST 1000
-- Second conviction, 10 days, first version: one-tenth of 1,000 is 100 a day, 1,000.
#ASSERT `Under section 1093(4), what is the most I can be fined for the offence of not resolving the inconsistency` `s 1093(4) the text read as one-tenth of level 5` TRUE 10 400 1000 EQUALS JUST 1000
-- Second conviction, 10 days, second version: one-tenth of the greater of 5,000 and 400 is 500 a day, 5,000.
#ASSERT `Under section 1093(4), what is the most I can be fined for the offence of not resolving the inconsistency` `s 1093(4) the text read as one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4` TRUE 10 400 1000 EQUALS JUST 5000
-- The text does not say which version applies: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 1093(4), what is the most I can be fined for the offence of not resolving the inconsistency` `s 1093(4) the text does not say which version applies` TRUE 10 400 1000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- The registrar may remove a document it accepted under s 1073 whose registration had no legal consequences.
#ASSERT `Under section 1094, may the registrar remove this material from the register` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Registration had legal consequences and the registrar is not satisfied the interest in removal outweighs: no.
#ASSERT `Under section 1094, may the registrar remove this material from the register` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Neither limb of s 1094(1) holds: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 1094, may the registrar remove this material from the register` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Removed other than by court order and I have sufficient interest: I may apply.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 1094AB(1), may I ask the court for consequential orders now that the registrar has removed material from the register` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE; the question asked whether I may ask the court, but the function answers whether the court may make the orders on the application
#ASSERT `Under section 1094AB(1), may the court make consequential orders on my application now that the registrar has removed material from the register` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I have no sufficient interest: not covered.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 1094AB(1), may I ask the court for consequential orders now that the registrar has removed material from the register` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING; the question asked whether I may ask the court, but the function answers whether the court may make the orders on the application
#ASSERT `Under section 1094AB(1), may the court make consequential orders on my application now that the registrar has removed material from the register` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Material derived from something the court declared invalid, the court directs removal, no exception: the registrar must remove it.
#ASSERT `Under section 1096, must the registrar remove material from the register under a court order` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The material was delivered under Part 15: section 1096 does not apply.
#ASSERT `Under section 1096, must the registrar remove material from the register under a court order` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The court has not directed removal: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 1096, must the registrar remove material from the register under a court order` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The court has ordered removal and is satisfied that public inspection may damage the company and that its interest outweighs: it may direct that the order be kept from the register.
#ASSERT `Under section 1097, may the court direct that its removal order, or a note about it, be kept from the public register` `s 1097(3) that the court's order not be available for public inspection as part of the register` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The company's interest in non-disclosure does not outweigh: the court shall not give the direction.
#ASSERT `Under section 1097, may the court direct that its removal order, or a note about it, be kept from the public register` `s 1097(3) that the court's order not be available for public inspection as part of the register` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No removal order has been made under s 1096: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 1097, may the court direct that its removal order, or a note about it, be kept from the public register` `s 1097(3) that the court's order not be available for public inspection as part of the register` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An enhanced disclosure document was removed: the registrar must publish notice.
#ASSERT `Under section 1098(1), must the registrar publish notice that an enhanced disclosure document has been removed from the register` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Some other material was removed: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 1098(1), must the registrar publish notice that an enhanced disclosure document has been removed from the register` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Application granted, not since ceased, not suspended: I am an authorised corporate service provider.
#ASSERT `Under section 1098A, am I an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Suspended: not one for the time being.
#ASSERT `Under section 1098A, am I an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An individual who is a relevant person, whose identity is verified, meeting the other requirements: may apply.
#ASSERT `Under section 1098B(1), may I apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An individual whose identity is not verified: the "if" limb is not met, so the Act does not decide whether I may apply.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 1098B(1), may I apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE; name-test sweep (fork F19): the question returns a function named for a grant or a power, its gate is "if", and a failed "if" gate answers NOTHING, not the text's own no; the other reading, JUST FALSE, is in the fork register
#ASSERT `Under section 1098B(1), may I apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A firm: the identity limb speaks only of an individual.
#ASSERT `Under section 1098B(1), may I apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a relevant person: the "if" limb is not met, so the Act does not decide whether I may apply.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 1098B(1), may I apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE; name-test sweep (fork F19): the question returns a function named for a grant or a power, its gate is "if", and a failed "if" gate answers NOTHING, not the text's own no; the other reading, JUST FALSE, is in the fork register
#ASSERT `Under section 1098B(1), may I apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- All four conditions met and I do not appear unfit: the registrar must grant.
#ASSERT `Under section 1098B(4), must the registrar grant my application to become an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- It appears I am not a fit and proper person: the registrar must refuse, so need not grant.
