#ASSERT `Under section 1132A(4), may regulations giving the registrar power to impose a financial penalty provide for a maximum penalty of this amount` 10001 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Exactly 10,000: the cap is not exceeded, and the Act does not itself grant the power.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 1132A(4), may the registrar's financial penalty be as much as this amount` 10000 EQUALS NOTHING; the question asked whether the registrar's penalty may be as much as the amount, but the function answers whether the regulations may provide for that maximum
#ASSERT `Under section 1132A(4), may regulations giving the registrar power to impose a financial penalty provide for a maximum penalty of this amount` 10000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- I have been given a financial penalty: the regulations must bar proceedings for that conduct.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 1132A(5), if I have been given a financial penalty for conduct, can I still be prosecuted for that conduct` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE; the question asked whether I can still be prosecuted, but the function states what the regulations must provide, so JUST TRUE meant the opposite of the question's yes
#ASSERT `Under section 1132A(5), must the regulations provide that no proceedings may be brought against me for conduct for which I have been given a financial penalty` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No financial penalty given: not covered.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 1132A(5), if I have been given a financial penalty for conduct, can I still be prosecuted for that conduct` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING; the question asked whether I can still be prosecuted, but the function states what the regulations must provide, so JUST TRUE meant the opposite of the question's yes
#ASSERT `Under section 1132A(5), must the regulations provide that no proceedings may be brought against me for conduct for which I have been given a financial penalty` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The offence was committed before commencement and the provision is not s 1132: Part 36 does not apply.
#ASSERT `Under section 1133, do the provisions of Part 36 apply to an offence I committed before they came into force` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The provision is s 1132: outside the sentence.
#ASSERT `Under section 1133, do the provisions of Part 36 apply to an offence I committed before they came into force` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Committed after commencement: the section does not say.
#ASSERT `Under section 1133, do the provisions of Part 36 apply to an offence I committed before they came into force` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part coa25 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa25-cases-seat.l4: cases for the seat layer coa25-seat.l4 (ss 1134 to 1157 and 1175 to 1208 of the Companies Act 2006).
-- One or more cases per question, with the facts a real person in the seat would state. Every expected value was decided
-- by reading the section and written down before the run, never copied from the encoding's output. A NOTHING is a "not
-- covered" case: the text does not decide it. The pounds are TEST numbers (the Act states neither the value of a level on
-- the standard scale nor "the general limit in a magistrates' court"). Mirror cases: the customer's question under
-- section 1202(2) and the business owner's under section 1205(1) are asked of the same failure and agree.
-- (Part 39, amendments and repeals of other Acts, and the regulation-making powers are machinery: no question, no case.)


-- ---- Company records (ss 1134 to 1138). A director of a small company asks how it must keep its registers.
#ASSERT `Under section 1134, is this document one of my company's company records` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a register the Companies Acts require
#ASSERT `Under section 1134, is this document one of my company's company records` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a register of debenture holders is a company record
#ASSERT `Under section 1134, is this document one of my company's company records` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no provision requires it: not a company record
#ASSERT `Under section 1135(1), may my company keep its records in this way` `hard copy form` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a bound register, arranged as the directors think fit, adequately recorded
#ASSERT `Under section 1135(1), may my company keep its records in this way` `electronic form` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not adequately recorded: the proviso fails
#ASSERT `Under section 1135(1), may my company keep its records in this way` `electronic form` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not arranged as the directors think fit: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1135(2), have my company's electronic records met the requirement that they can be reproduced in hard copy form` `electronic form` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- electronic records that can be printed
#ASSERT `Under section 1135(2), have my company's electronic records met the requirement that they can be reproduced in hard copy form` `electronic form` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- electronic records that cannot be printed
#ASSERT `Under section 1135(3), am I guilty of an offence, as an officer of my company, because of how it keeps its records` `electronic form` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- electronic records that cannot be printed; I am an officer in default
#ASSERT `Under section 1135(3), am I guilty of an offence, as an officer of my company, because of how it keeps its records` `electronic form` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the records can be printed: the company complied
#ASSERT `Under section 1135(3), am I guilty of an offence, as an officer of my company, because of how it keeps its records` `electronic form` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- I am not an officer in default: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1135(4), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)` 1000 EQUALS `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines` OF (JUST 1000), (JUST 100) -- test pounds for level 3: first conviction, and one-tenth for each day
#ASSERT `Under section 1135(5), is an old instrument that requires the debenture register in hard copy now read as allowing electronic form` (Date 11 2 1979) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an instrument made the day before 12 February 1979
#ASSERT `Under section 1135(5), is an old instrument that requires the debenture register in hard copy now read as allowing electronic form` (Date 12 2 1979) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- made on 12 February 1979: not "before"
#ASSERT `Under section 1136(6), does keeping my company's records at this place satisfy the requirement to keep them available for inspection` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not all the records are kept at the specified place
#ASSERT `Under section 1136(6), does keeping my company's records at this place satisfy the requirement to keep them available for inspection` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- all kept there: the regulations decide the rest
#ASSERT `Under section 1137(5)(b), is my company prevented by the Act or the regulations from charging less than the prescribed fee for inspection or copies, or nothing at all` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the Act and the regulations do not stop the company charging less, or nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 1137(5)(b), is my company prevented by the Act or the regulations from charging less than the prescribed fee for inspection or copies, or nothing at all` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- no fee may be charged: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1138(1), has my company taken the precautions against falsification of its records that the Act requires` `s 1138 another company record` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- records on loose sheets; precautions guard against falsification but do not help discover it
#ASSERT `Under section 1138(1), has my company taken the precautions against falsification of its records that the Act requires` `s 1138 another company record` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- bound books: the duty does not engage
#ASSERT `Under section 1138(1), has my company taken the precautions against falsification of its records that the Act requires` `s 1138 a copy of a director's service contract or a memorandum of its terms (s 228)` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an s 228 document: the section does not apply
#ASSERT `Under section 1138(2), am I guilty of an offence, as an officer of my company, because its records are not protected against falsification` `s 1138 another company record` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- no precaution against falsification; I am an officer in default
#ASSERT `Under section 1138(2), am I guilty of an offence, as an officer of my company, because its records are not protected against falsification` `s 1138 another company record` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- both precautions taken: no failure
#ASSERT `Under section 1138(3), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)` 1000 EQUALS `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines` OF (JUST 1000), (JUST 100) -- test pounds for level 3

-- ---- Service addresses (ss 1139 to 1142). A director asks how documents reach the company and her.
#ASSERT `Under section 1139(1), is a document validly served on my company if it is left at, or posted to, its registered office` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- left at the registered office
#ASSERT `Under section 1139(1), is a document validly served on my company if it is left at, or posted to, its registered office` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- delivered some other way: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1139(2), is a document validly served on an overseas company registered under section 1046` "first text" TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- first text, paragraph (a): left with a resident authorised person
#ASSERT `Under section 1139(2), is a document validly served on an overseas company registered under section 1046` "first text" TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- first text, paragraph (b) is an "if" that is not met: an authorised person exists and accepts service
#ASSERT `Under section 1139(2), is a document validly served on an overseas company registered under section 1046` "first text" TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- first text, paragraph (b): no such person, so a place of business in the United Kingdom
#ASSERT `Under section 1139(2), is a document validly served on an overseas company registered under section 1046` "second text" TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- second text, paragraph (a): the company's own registered address
#ASSERT `Under section 1139(2), is a document validly served on an overseas company registered under section 1046` "neither" TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the question names no text of section 1139(2): not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1139(4), is court process validly served on my company, registered in Scotland or Northern Ireland, at its principal place of business in England and Wales` Scotland TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a Scottish company served at its English principal place of business, addressed to the head officer
#ASSERT `Under section 1139(4), is court process validly served on my company, registered in Scotland or Northern Ireland, at its principal place of business in England and Wales` `England and Wales` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- registered in England and Wales: outside section 1139(4)
#ASSERT `Under section 1139(4), have I, as the person who issued the process, sent the company's registered office the copy the Act requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- I sent the copy to the registered office
#ASSERT `Under section 1139(4), have I, as the person who issued the process, sent the company's registered office the copy the Act requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- I did not send the copy
#ASSERT `Under section 1140(1), is a document validly served on me, as a director, secretary or other registered person, at my registered address` `s 1140 a director or secretary of a company` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a director: left at my registered address shown in the public register
#ASSERT `Under section 1140(1), is a document validly served on me, as a director, secretary or other registered person, at my registered address` `s 1140 a director or secretary of a company` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- my appointment ended and the address is registered for no other appointment: service may not be effected
#ASSERT `Under section 1140(1), is a document validly served on me, as a director, secretary or other registered person, at my registered address` `s 1140 another kind of person` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a person section 1140 does not list: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1140(5), a document was served at my previous address after I changed it: is the service still valid` (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 23 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the 14th day of the period that begins with the day notice of the change was registered
#ASSERT `Under section 1140(5), a document was served at my previous address after I changed it: is the service still valid` (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 24 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day after the 14 days
#ASSERT `Under section 1141, is this address a service address for me` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- documents can be effectively served there
#ASSERT `Under section 1141, is this address a service address for me` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- they cannot
#ASSERT `Under section 1142, must the address I am asked to give be a service address` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an obligation to give my address: a service address
#ASSERT `Under section 1142, must the address I am asked to give be a service address` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- the Act expressly provides otherwise

-- ---- Sending or supplying documents or information (ss 1143 to 1148). A shareholder asks about paper copies and when electronic notices count as received.
#ASSERT `Under section 1144, has the document or information I sent to, or received from, a company been sent or supplied as the Act requires` `s 1144 to a company by a person who is not a company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- I sent a document to the company in accordance with Schedule 4
#ASSERT `Under section 1144, has the document or information I sent to, or received from, a company been sent or supplied as the Act requires` `s 1144 by a company to a person who is not a company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the company sent me a document but not in accordance with Schedule 5
#ASSERT `Under section 1145(1), as a member or debenture holder, can I require my company to send me a hard copy of a document it sent me electronically` `s 1145 a member of the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a member who got a document by e-mail
#ASSERT `Under section 1145(1), as a member or debenture holder, can I require my company to send me a hard copy of a document it sent me electronically` `s 1145 another person` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- neither a member nor a debenture holder
#ASSERT `Under section 1145(2), by what date must my company send me the hard copy I asked for` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS (Date 22 3 2026) -- the company received my request on 1 March 2026: 21 days
#ASSERT `Under section 1145(2), did my company send me the hard copy in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 22 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- sent on the last day
#ASSERT `Under section 1145(2), did my company send me the hard copy in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 23 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- sent a day late
#ASSERT `Under section 1145(3), may my company charge me for the hard copy version I asked for` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the company may not charge for the version I am entitled to require
#ASSERT `Under section 1145(3), may my company charge me for the hard copy version I asked for` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a version I am entitled to require under (1)
#ASSERT `Under section 1145(4), am I guilty of an offence, as an officer of my company, because it did not send a requested hard copy as the Act requires` `s 1145 a member of the company` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 25 3 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- sent on 25 March: late; I am an officer in default
#ASSERT `Under section 1145(4), am I guilty of an offence, as an officer of my company, because it did not send a requested hard copy as the Act requires` `s 1145 a member of the company` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- sent in time: the company complied
#ASSERT `Under section 1145(5), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)` 1000 EQUALS `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines` OF (JUST 1000), (JUST 100) -- test pounds for level 3
#ASSERT `Under section 1146, is the document or information I sent to a company sufficiently authenticated` `hard copy form` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a signed letter
#ASSERT `Under section 1146, is the document or information I sent to a company sufficiently authenticated` `electronic form` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an e-mail whose sender's identity was confirmed in the manner the company specified
#ASSERT `Under section 1146, is the document or information I sent to a company sufficiently authenticated` `electronic form` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no manner specified; a statement of identity but the company has reason to doubt it
#ASSERT `Under section 1147, on what day is a document my company sent me treated as received` `s 1147 by post to an address in the United Kingdom` TRUE (Date 2 1 2026) 10 (Date 1 1 2026) 0 EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 6 1 2026) -- posted on Friday 2 January 2026 at 10:00: 14 hours on Friday, 24 on Monday, 10 on Tuesday
#ASSERT `Under section 1147, on what day is a document my company sent me treated as received` `s 1147 by post to an address in the United Kingdom` TRUE (Date 2 1 2026) 10 (Date 1 1 2026) 0 (LIST (Date 5 1 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 7 1 2026) -- the same posting with Monday 5 January a bank holiday
#ASSERT `Under section 1147, on what day is a document my company sent me treated as received` `s 1147 by means of a website` TRUE (Date 5 1 2026) 9 (Date 7 1 2026) 8 EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 7 1 2026) -- a website: the later of the material being made available and notice of it
#ASSERT `Under section 1147, on what day is a document my company sent me treated as received` `s 1147 in another way` TRUE (Date 5 1 2026) 9 (Date 7 1 2026) 8 EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING -- sent in another way: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1148(1), is this a document for the purposes of the company communications provisions` `s 1148 a notice` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a notice is a "document"
#ASSERT `Under section 1148(1), is this a document for the purposes of the company communications provisions` `s 1148 any other document` EQUALS NOTHING -- the list is not closed: "includes"

-- ---- Requirements as to independent valuation (ss 1149 to 1153). Only if you are asked to value non-cash consideration, or are an officer asked for information.
#ASSERT `Under section 1150(1), may I make the valuation and report on non-cash consideration for a company` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an eligible statutory auditor with no tie to the company
#ASSERT `Under section 1150(1), may I make the valuation and report on non-cash consideration for a company` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- an employee of the company is not independent
#ASSERT `Under section 1150(1), may I make the valuation and report on non-cash consideration for a company` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not eligible as a statutory auditor
#ASSERT `Under section 1151(1), do I meet the independence requirement for valuing a company's non-cash consideration` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- no disqualifying tie
#ASSERT `Under section 1151(1), do I meet the independence requirement for valuing a company's non-cash consideration` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a regulations connection exists
#ASSERT `Under section 1152(2), is this person my associate for the independence requirement` `s 1152 the individual's spouse or civil partner or minor child or step-child` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- my spouse is my associate
#ASSERT `Under section 1152(2), is this person my associate for the independence requirement` `s 1152 none of these relationships to the individual` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- an adult friend is not
#ASSERT `Under section 1153(1), may the valuer require information and explanation from me, as an officer of the company` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the valuer may require what he thinks necessary
#ASSERT `Under section 1153(1), may the valuer require information and explanation from me, as an officer of the company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not information he thinks necessary: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1153(2), have I committed an offence by what I told a valuer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a reckless, misleading statement to the valuer
#ASSERT `Under section 1153(2), have I committed an offence by what I told a valuer` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not made to a person valuing: subsection (2) does not reach it
#ASSERT `Under section 1153(4), what penalty can I face for making a false statement to a valuer` `on summary conviction in Scotland` EQUALS JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 6, unit IS Months), `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE) -- six months or the statutory maximum or both

-- ---- Notice of appointment of certain officers, courts and legal proceedings (ss 1154 to 1157). Only if you were appointed judicial factor, interim manager or manager, or are sued for breach of duty.
#ASSERT `Under section 1154(1) and (2), who must give the registrar notice of my appointment` `s 1154 a judicial factor appointed in relation to a company (in Scotland)` EQUALS JUST `s 1154 the judicial factor` -- a judicial factor gives the notice himself
#ASSERT `Under section 1154(1) and (2), who must give the registrar notice of my appointment` `s 1154 another appointment in relation to a company` EQUALS NOTHING -- another appointment: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1155(1), have I committed an offence as a judicial factor by not telling the registrar of my appointment within 14 days` (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE (Date 15 6 2026) (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- notice given on the 14th day after my appointment
#ASSERT `Under section 1155(1), have I committed an offence as a judicial factor by not telling the registrar of my appointment within 14 days` (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE (Date 16 6 2026) (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- notice given on the 15th day after: an offence
#ASSERT `Under section 1155(1), have I committed an offence as a judicial factor by not telling the registrar of my appointment within 14 days` (Date 1 6 2026) FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 10 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING -- no notice yet, and the 14 days have not run out
#ASSERT `Under section 1155(2), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)` 5000 EQUALS `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines` OF (JUST 5000), (JUST 500) -- test pounds for level 5: first conviction, and one-tenth for each day
#ASSERT `Under section 1156(1), which courts are the court for my company` Scotland EQUALS LIST `s 1156 the Court of Session`, `s 1156 the sheriff court` -- for a company registered in Scotland
#ASSERT `Under section 1157(1), as an officer or auditor sued for breach of duty, can the court relieve me from liability` `s 1157 an officer of a company` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a director sued for breach of duty who acted honestly and reasonably and ought fairly to be excused
#ASSERT `Under section 1157(1), as an officer or auditor sued for breach of duty, can the court relieve me from liability` `s 1157 an officer of a company` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 1157(1), as an officer or auditor sued for breach of duty, can the court relieve me from liability` `s 1157 an officer of a company` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- he did not act honestly and reasonably; the court may relieve "if it appears" that he acted honestly and reasonably, and a power whose "if" gate is unmet answers NOTHING (fork F19)
#ASSERT `Under section 1157(1), as an officer or auditor sued for breach of duty, can the court relieve me from liability` `s 1157 another person` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- neither an officer nor an auditor: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1157(2), may I apply to the court for relief now, because I fear a claim` `s 1157 an officer of a company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- I fear a claim: I may apply now
#ASSERT `Under section 1157(2), may I apply to the court for relief now, because I fear a claim` `s 1157 an officer of a company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no reason to apprehend a claim: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1157(3), in a jury trial, may the judge direct judgment for me because I ought to be relieved` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a jury trial and the judge is satisfied I ought to be relieved
#ASSERT `Under section 1157(3), in a jury trial, may the judge direct judgment for me because I ought to be relieved` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no jury: the "Where" fails

-- ---- Company directors: foreign disqualification etc (ss 1182 to 1191). Only if you are subject to restrictions abroad.
#ASSERT `Under section 1182(2), am I subject to foreign restrictions because of a disqualification or undertaking abroad` TRUE `s 1182 being a director of a company` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- disqualified abroad by reason of misconduct from being a director
#ASSERT `Under section 1182(2), am I subject to foreign restrictions because of a disqualification or undertaking abroad` TRUE `s 1182 being a director of a company` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no disqualification, condition or undertaking
#ASSERT `Under section 1182(2), am I subject to foreign restrictions because of a disqualification or undertaking abroad` FALSE `s 1182 being a director of a company` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not under the law of a country outside the United Kingdom
#ASSERT `Under section 1184(4), am I a person disqualified under this Part` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- disqualified automatically by the regulations
#ASSERT `Under section 1184(4), am I a person disqualified under this Part` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- none of the three
#ASSERT `Under section 1186(2), what is the most the regulations may provide as a penalty for acting in breach of a disqualification` `on conviction on indictment` (Date 1 1 2026) 12 EQUALS JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 2, unit IS Years), `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE) -- two years or a fine or both
#ASSERT `Under section 1186(2), what is the most the regulations may provide as a penalty for acting in breach of a disqualification` `on summary conviction in England and Wales` (Date 1 5 2022) 12 EQUALS JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 6, unit IS Months), `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE) -- an offence on 1 May 2022: six months
#ASSERT `Under section 1186(2), what is the most the regulations may provide as a penalty for acting in breach of a disqualification` `on summary conviction in England and Wales` (Date 2 5 2022) 12 EQUALS JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 12, unit IS Months), `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE) -- an offence on 2 May 2022: the general limit, here a TEST 12 months
#ASSERT `Under section 1191(2), what is the most the regulations may provide as a penalty for failing to send, or falsifying, a statement to the registrar` `on summary conviction` (Date 1 1 2026) 12 EQUALS NOTHING -- the part of the United Kingdom is not stated: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1187(2), am I jointly and severally liable for a company's debts under regulations made under section 1187` TRUE `s 1187 the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- jointly and severally liable with the company
#ASSERT `Under section 1187(2), am I jointly and severally liable for a company's debts under regulations made under section 1187` FALSE `s 1187 the company` EQUALS NOTHING -- not made personally responsible by the regulations
#ASSERT `Under section 1187(3), am I involved in the management of a company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- concerned indirectly in the management
#ASSERT `Under section 1187(3), am I involved in the management of a company` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- neither concerned in nor taking part in the management

-- ---- Business names: restricted or prohibited names (ss 1192 to 1199A). For an individual who carries on business, or a director of a company that does.
#ASSERT `Under section 1192(2), does the Act stop me trading under my own surname with the additions I have` `s 1192 an individual carrying on business` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- my surname with my forename: the Chapter does not prevent it
#ASSERT `Under section 1192(2), does the Act stop me trading under my own surname with the additions I have` `s 1192 an individual carrying on business` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- my surname with an addition that is not permitted: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1193(1), am I breaking the Act by trading under a name that suggests a connection with government or a public authority` TRUE `s 1193 a local authority` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- trading as "Greentown Council Services" without approval
#ASSERT `Under section 1193(1), am I breaking the Act by trading under a name that suggests a connection with government or a public authority` TRUE `s 1193 a local authority` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- with the approval of the Secretary of State: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1193(1), am I breaking the Act by trading under a name that suggests a connection with government or a public authority` TRUE `s 1193 a local authority` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- my business predates the Chapter under its lawful name: sections 1192 to 1197 do not apply
#ASSERT `Under section 1193(1), am I breaking the Act by trading under a name that suggests a connection with government or a public authority` TRUE `s 1193 a local authority` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the Secretary of State gave me a notice lifting the prohibition
#ASSERT `Under section 1193(4), am I guilty of an offence for trading under a name that suggests a connection with government or a public authority` TRUE `s 1193 a local authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an offence
#ASSERT `Under section 1193(4), am I guilty of an offence for trading under a name that suggests a connection with government or a public authority` TRUE `s 1193 no such body` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the name suggests no such connection: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1193(6), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)` 1000 EQUALS `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines` OF (JUST 1000), (JUST 100) -- test pounds for level 3
#ASSERT `Under section 1194(1), am I breaking the Act by trading under a name that includes a specified word or expression without the Secretary of State's approval` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a specified word without approval
#ASSERT `Under section 1194(1), am I breaking the Act by trading under a name that includes a specified word or expression without the Secretary of State's approval` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no specified word: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1194(5), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)` 1000 EQUALS `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines` OF (JUST 1000), (JUST 100) -- test pounds for level 3
#ASSERT `Under section 1195(2), have I asked the department or body for its view, as an applicant for approval must` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- I asked the department in writing
#ASSERT `Under section 1195(2), have I asked the department or body for its view, as an applicant for approval must` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- I did not
#ASSERT `Under section 1195(3), have I sent the Secretary of State the statement and any response, as an applicant for approval must` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- statement and copy of the response sent
#ASSERT `Under section 1195(3), have I sent the Secretary of State the statement and any response, as an applicant for approval must` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a response came and I sent no copy
#ASSERT `Under section 1195(4), may the Secretary of State refuse to consider my application for approval` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- I never asked the department: the Secretary of State may refuse to consider the application
#ASSERT `Under section 1195(4), may the Secretary of State refuse to consider my application for approval` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- both requirements met: the power to refuse does not arise
#ASSERT `Under section 1196(3), has the Secretary of State's approval of my name been withdrawn as from today` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- withdrawn as from the date stated: on that date
#ASSERT `Under section 1196(3), has the Secretary of State's approval of my name been withdrawn as from today` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day before the date stated
#ASSERT `Under section 1196(2), may the Secretary of State withdraw the approval of my name by notice` `s 1196 an approval given for the purposes of s 1193 (name suggesting connection with government or public authority)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- overriding considerations of public policy
#ASSERT `Under section 1196(2), may the Secretary of State withdraw the approval of my name by notice` `s 1196 another approval` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not an approval under s 1193 or s 1194
#ASSERT `Under section 1196A(1), am I breaking the Act by trading under a name that falsely suggests a connection with a foreign government or an international organisation` TRUE `s 1196A a foreign government or an agency or authority of a foreign government` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a name that falsely suggests a foreign government connection
#ASSERT `Under section 1196A(1), am I breaking the Act by trading under a name that falsely suggests a connection with a foreign government or an international organisation` TRUE `s 1196A a foreign government or an agency or authority of a foreign government` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a Secretary of State notice lifts the prohibition
#ASSERT `Under section 1196A(4), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)` 1000 EQUALS `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines` OF (JUST 1000), (JUST 100) -- test pounds for level 3
#ASSERT `Under section 1197(5), am I guilty of an offence for using a name that regulations under section 1197 prohibit` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a name the regulations prohibit
#ASSERT `Under section 1197(5), am I guilty of an offence for using a name that regulations under section 1197 prohibit` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the regulations do not prohibit it: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1197(7), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)` 1000 EQUALS `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines` OF (JUST 1000), (JUST 100) -- test pounds for level 3
#ASSERT `Under section 1198(1), is my business name so misleading about what the business does that it breaks the Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- so misleading as to pose a risk of harm to the public
#ASSERT `Under section 1198(1), is my business name so misleading about what the business does that it breaks the Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not so misleading: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1198(4), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)` 1000 EQUALS `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines` OF (JUST 1000), (JUST 100) -- test pounds for level 3
#ASSERT `Under section 1198A(1), is my company breaking the Act by carrying on business under the name it was directed or ordered to change` `s 1198A a direction under s 67` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- directed under s 67 to change its name and still trading under it
#ASSERT `Under section 1198A(1), is my company breaking the Act by carrying on business under the name it was directed or ordered to change` `s 1198A a direction under s 67` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the period for complying has not expired
#ASSERT `Under section 1198A(1), is my company breaking the Act by carrying on business under the name it was directed or ordered to change` `s 1198A another direction` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not a relevant direction and no s 73 order: the "Where" fails
#ASSERT `Under section 1198A(4), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)` 1000 EQUALS `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines` OF (JUST 1000), (JUST 100) -- test pounds for level 3
#ASSERT `Under section 1198B(1), is my company breaking the Act by carrying on business under a name that another company was directed or ordered to change` `s 1198A a direction under s 67` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- another company was directed to change a name I now use; the same person ran both
#ASSERT `Under section 1198B(1), is my company breaking the Act by carrying on business under a name that another company was directed or ordered to change` `s 1198A a direction under s 67` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- my company is registered by that name: an exception
#ASSERT `Under section 1198B(1), is my company breaking the Act by carrying on business under a name that another company was directed or ordered to change` `s 1198A a direction under s 67` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no person has a relevant relationship with both
#ASSERT `Under section 1198B(1), is my company breaking the Act by carrying on business under a name that another company was directed or ordered to change` `s 1198A a direction under s 76` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a direction under s 76 is not a relevant direction for s 1198B (a finding)
#ASSERT `Under section 1198B(6), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)` 1000 EQUALS `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines` OF (JUST 1000), (JUST 100) -- test pounds for level 3
#ASSERT `Under section 1199(3), do sections 1192 to 1197 not apply to my business, carried on under its existing lawful name, on a date within twelve months of my taking it over` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 14 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the last day of the twelve months
#ASSERT `Under section 1199(3), do sections 1192 to 1197 not apply to my business, carried on under its existing lawful name, on a date within twelve months of my taking it over` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day after
#ASSERT `Under section 1199A(1), do the prohibitions of Chapter 1 not apply to the business I carry on under my name, because the Secretary of State has given me a written notice` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a notice on national security grounds
#ASSERT `Under section 1199A(1), do the prohibitions of Chapter 1 not apply to the business I carry on under my name, because the Secretary of State has given me a written notice` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a notice was given but the Secretary of State was satisfied of neither ground: a grant whose gate fails is not covered (fork F25)
#ASSERT `Under section 1199A(1), do the prohibitions of Chapter 1 not apply to the business I carry on under my name, because the Secretary of State has given me a written notice` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- no notice given: not covered

-- ---- Business names: disclosure by an individual or partnership (ss 1200 to 1208). Asked by the individual or partner who carries on the business, and by a customer or supplier who deals with it.
#ASSERT `Under section 1200(2), is the name I trade under a business name` `s 1200 an individual` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- my surname alone is not a "business name"
#ASSERT `Under section 1200(2), is the name I trade under a business name` `s 1200 an individual` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a trading name that is not my surname
#ASSERT `Under section 1201(1), does what I disclose contain the information Chapter 2 requires` `s 1200 an individual` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- name and an address for service
#ASSERT `Under section 1201(1), does what I disclose contain the information Chapter 2 requires` `s 1200 an individual` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no address for service
#ASSERT `Under section 1201(2), does the address I give meet the requirement to be in the United Kingdom where I have a place of business there` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a place of business in the United Kingdom and a United Kingdom address
#ASSERT `Under section 1201(2), does the address I give meet the requirement to be in the United Kingdom where I have a place of business there` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- an address abroad
#ASSERT `Under section 1201(3), does the address I give meet the requirement of physical delivery and an acknowledgement of delivery where I have no place of business in the United Kingdom` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- no place of business here: an address with physical delivery and an acknowledgement
#ASSERT `Under section 1201(3), does the address I give meet the requirement of physical delivery and an acknowledgement of delivery where I have no place of business in the United Kingdom` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no acknowledgement of delivery
#ASSERT `Under section 1202(1), have I complied with the requirement to state my details, in legible characters, on this business document` `s 1202 a business letter` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- my details are on the letter
#ASSERT `Under section 1202(1), have I complied with the requirement to state my details, in legible characters, on this business document` `s 1202 an invoice or receipt issued in the course of the business` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- my details are missing from the invoice
#ASSERT `Under section 1202(1), have I complied with the requirement to state my details, in legible characters, on this business document` `s 1202 another document` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- a kind of document the Act does not list: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1202(1), have I complied with the requirement to state my details, in legible characters, on this business document` `s 1202 a business letter` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a large partnership meeting section 1203: the requirement does not apply
#ASSERT `Under section 1202(2), did the business I dealt with give me its owner's details when I asked, as the Act requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the customer's question: I asked, and was given the details immediately in writing
#ASSERT `Under section 1202(2), did the business I dealt with give me its owner's details when I asked, as the Act requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the customer's question: I asked, and was not given them immediately
#ASSERT `Under section 1203(1), is a document issued by our partnership of more than 20 persons exempt from the requirement to state the partners' names` 21 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a partnership of 21 meeting all three conditions
#ASSERT `Under section 1203(1), is a document issued by our partnership of more than 20 persons exempt from the requirement to state the partners' names` 20 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- twenty is not more than twenty
#ASSERT `Under section 1203(1), is a document issued by our partnership of more than 20 persons exempt from the requirement to state the partners' names` 21 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no list of partners kept
#ASSERT `Under section 1203(3), may I inspect the list of partners' names of a large partnership` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- I may inspect the list during office hours
#ASSERT `Under section 1203(3), may I inspect the list of partners' names of a large partnership` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no list is maintained for the purposes of section 1203
#ASSERT `Under section 1203(4), have I, as a member of a partnership, committed an offence by refusing an inspection` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- I refused an inspection without reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `Under section 1203(4), have I, as a member of a partnership, committed an offence by refusing an inspection` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- I had a reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `Under section 1203(5), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)` 1000 EQUALS `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines` OF (JUST 1000), (JUST 100) -- test pounds for level 3
#ASSERT `Under section 1204(1), have I complied with the requirement to display a notice of my details at my business premises` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- my shop is open to customers and shows no notice
#ASSERT `Under section 1204(1), have I complied with the requirement to display a notice of my details at my business premises` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- notice displayed prominently
#ASSERT `Under section 1204(1), have I complied with the requirement to display a notice of my details at my business premises` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- premises where the business is not carried on: the requirement does not apply
#ASSERT `Under section 1204(1), have I complied with the requirement to display a notice of my details at my business premises` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- premises the business uses but to which no customer or supplier has access: the requirement does not apply (fork F24)
#ASSERT `Under section 1205(1), have I committed an offence by not making the disclosure Chapter 2 requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- my invoices omit my details; no reasonable excuse (a MIRROR of the 1202(2) customer cases above: a failed duty and an offence agree)
#ASSERT `Under section 1205(1), have I committed an offence by not making the disclosure Chapter 2 requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- every requirement met: no offence
#ASSERT `Under section 1205(1), have I committed an offence by not making the disclosure Chapter 2 requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- a reasonable excuse: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1205(3), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)` 1000 EQUALS `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines` OF (JUST 1000), (JUST 100) -- test pounds for level 3
#ASSERT `Under section 1206(2), must the court dismiss a claim brought against me by a business that did not make the disclosure Chapter 2 requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- sued by a business that hid its identity; I have an unpursuable claim: the court must dismiss
#ASSERT `Under section 1206(2), must the court dismiss a claim brought against me by a business that did not make the disclosure Chapter 2 requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the court is satisfied that it is just and equitable to let the proceedings continue
#ASSERT `Under section 1206(2), must the court dismiss a claim brought against me by a business that did not make the disclosure Chapter 2 requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the claimant is not within Chapter 2: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1207, do the general provisions about offences apply to an offence under Part 41` TRUE 1121 EQUALS JUST TRUE -- section 1121 (officer in default) applies
#ASSERT `Under section 1207, do the general provisions about offences apply to an offence under Part 41` TRUE 1124 EQUALS NOTHING -- section 1124 is not named: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 1208, is this arrangement a partnership for Part 41` `s 1208 a limited partnership registered under the Limited Partnerships Act 1907` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a limited partnership is a partnership
#ASSERT `Under section 1208, is this arrangement a partnership for Part 41` `s 1208 another arrangement` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a company is not

