§ `Cases for the individual's questions (Part 42)`

-- s 1210(1). Order: Part 16, Building Societies Act, friendly society, society is an insurer, society is an issuer, Lloyd's regulations, insurance undertaking, prescribed.
-- Priya was appointed auditor of a company under Part 16.
#ASSERT `Under section 1210(1), am I a statutory auditor` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Tom was appointed auditor of a friendly society that is an insurer: a statutory auditor.
#ASSERT `Under section 1210(1), am I a statutory auditor` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Tom's friendly society is neither an insurer nor an issuer on a UK regulated market: not a statutory auditor on that route.
#ASSERT `Under section 1210(1), am I a statutory auditor` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Ana audits a company's accounts by private engagement only: not appointed on any listed route.
#ASSERT `Under section 1210(1), am I a statutory auditor` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A person appointed of a prescribed person under a prescribed enactment.
#ASSERT `Under section 1210(1), am I a statutory auditor` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 1210(2)
#ASSERT `Under section 1210(2), is the company or other person I run an audited person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 1210(2), is the company or other person I run an audited person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 1210(2), is the company or other person I run an audited person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

