#ASSERT `Under section 1212(1), is the individual or firm eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 1212(1), is the individual or firm eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 1212(1), is the individual or firm eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 1211. Order: subject to rules, body recognised, eligible under rules, I am an Auditor General, a suspension notice suspends my eligibility.
-- Eligible by virtue of Chapter 2: the overview does not itself say so, so it is not covered here.
#ASSERT `Under section 1211, can I be eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor at all` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not eligible by either Chapter: "only if" says no.
#ASSERT `Under section 1211, can I be eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor at all` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An Auditor General with no suspension notice is eligible by virtue of Chapter 3: not ruled out.
#ASSERT `Under section 1211, can I be eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor at all` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An Auditor General whose eligibility is suspended: section 1226(2) is subject to the notice, so not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 1211, can I be eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor at all` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

