#ASSERT `Under schedule 1C paragraph 13(1), is the time allowed for acceptance within the limits the rules must ensure` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 13 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1C paragraph 13(1), is the time allowed for acceptance within the limits the rules must ensure` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 14 1 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 17(1): columns: the day; the board received the information; an earlier stage fixed; that date; the result made public; that date; only seeking alternative bids; may frustrate; share issue
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1C paragraph 17(1), must the rules require our board to obtain a general meeting's prior authorisation before the action` (Date 1 2 2025) (Date 10 1 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) TRUE (Date 20 2 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- after the result is made public the relevant period has ended
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1C paragraph 17(1), must the rules require our board to obtain a general meeting's prior authorisation before the action` (Date 21 2 2025) (Date 10 1 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) TRUE (Date 20 2 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- seeking alternative takeover bids is excepted
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1C paragraph 17(1), must the rules require our board to obtain a general meeting's prior authorisation before the action` (Date 1 2 2025) (Date 10 1 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) TRUE (Date 20 2 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- an action that may not frustrate the bid and is not a share issue is not covered
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1C paragraph 17(1), must the rules require our board to obtain a general meeting's prior authorisation before the action` (Date 1 2 2025) (Date 10 1 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) TRUE (Date 20 2 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1C paragraph 18(1), has the board met the requirement to draw up and make public its opinion` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1C paragraph 18(1), has the board met the requirement to draw up and make public its opinion` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 20(1) and 20(3): a bid made by the company itself is not a takeover bid
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1C paragraph 20(1), is the offer a takeover bid` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1C paragraph 20(1), is the offer a takeover bid` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1C paragraph 20(3), am I a person acting in concert` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1C paragraph 20(3), am I a person acting in concert` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- Not-covered cases for the questions that can answer NOTHING on the inputs they take
-- Each expected value was decided from the provision before running.
-- Schedule 1 paragraph 3: neither route holds and no cessation applies: JUST FALSE, which says only that paragraph 3 does not give the interest (paragraph 2(1) says an interest of any kind counts, so other paragraphs may)
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1 paragraph 3, am I taken to have an interest in the shares by virtue of paragraph 3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (Schedule 1 paragraph 3 is not in this list: when neither route holds the layer-1 gathering answers JUST FALSE by the failed-"if" reading, marginal reading M1, so the question cannot answer NOTHING on plain inputs.)
-- Schedule 1A paragraph 3: 20 votes of 100 are held, and 6 more are held in a way the person is unsure counts: 20% is not more than 25%, 26% is, so the text does not decide
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1A paragraph 3, do I hold, directly or indirectly, more than 25% of the voting rights in the company` TRUE 20 0 0 0 0 0 0 6 100 0 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Schedule 1B paragraph 3(4): the agreement is not one to transfer an associated right, not in a liquidation, and not on a court order: the paragraph says nothing of it
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1B paragraph 3(4), is my agreement to transfer the associated right void` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Schedule 1B paragraphs 5(3) and 5(4): a direction under paragraph 4 or 8 covers what the person did, and the paragraphs are subject to it
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1B paragraph 5(3), do I commit an offence by not notifying a person entitled to vote` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1B paragraph 5(4), do I commit an offence by entering into a void agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Schedule 1B paragraph 13(3): a summary conviction in no named place: the paragraph distinguishes England and Wales, Scotland and Northern Ireland
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1B paragraph 13(3), what is the penalty for failing to comply with a notice` `on summary conviction` 6 EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- Questions that cannot answer NOTHING on the inputs they take
-- These questions take only yes/no answers, dates or numbers, and the rule they call answers JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE (or a number) for every such input, so there is no
-- not-covered case to assert: schedule 1 paragraphs 3, 4 and 5; schedule 1A paragraphs 5, 8(1) and 18(3); schedule 1B paragraphs 1(3), 8(3), 10(3), 11, 13(1), 14(1) and 14B(1) (4(1) can answer NOTHING since the name-test sweep of 2026-11-12: see its case above);
-- schedule 1C paragraphs 5, 7(1), 8(2), 9(2), 12(4), 18(1), 20(1) and 20(3); sections 1282 (both questions that return a rank or an amount), 1283, 1288, 1291(1)(b) and 1299.
-- The layer-1 functions have `NOTHING` branches only where a `MAYBE BOOLEAN` input they take is itself `NOTHING` (for example schedule 1A paragraph 8(2) feeding 8(1)); the seat
-- asks those facts as yes/no, so the branch is not reachable from here.

-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part coa29 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa29-cases-seat.l4: cases for coa29-seat.l4, the seat layer for Schedules 2 to 9 of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom).
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member of a company registered under the Act, or who
-- deals with one. Generated by work/gen_cases_seat.py. Each case states the facts a real person in the seat would state and an answer written by
-- hand from the Schedule's own words (named in the comment above the case); none is copied from the encoding's output. Every question of the
-- seat layer has at least one case; where a question can answer yes, no and null, each is a case.


§§ `Schedule 2 -- the Takeover Panel's disclosures (a group the person asks only if the Panel holds information about them)`

-- Part 1 para 4 of group (A) lists the Bank of England.
-- the Panel would tell the Bank of England
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 1, is the person the Takeover Panel would tell one of the persons specified there` WITH `recipient` IS `sch 2 part 1(A) para 4 the Bank of England`, `the person meets the meaning the entry borrows from another Act` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Part 1 lists no private company that is not a public body; the Part is a closed list handed to by s 948(3)(b) (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)).
-- the Panel would tell someone not listed
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 1, is the person the Takeover Panel would tell one of the persons specified there` WITH `recipient` IS `sch 2 part 1 none of the persons listed`, `the person meets the meaning the entry borrows from another Act` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Group (B) para 8 names a police officer 'within the meaning of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954'.
-- a Jersey police officer, within that Law's meaning
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 1, is the person the Takeover Panel would tell one of the persons specified there` WITH `recipient` IS `sch 2 part 1(B) para 8 a police officer within the meaning of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954`, `the person meets the meaning the entry borrows from another Act` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- named as a Jersey police officer but not within that Law's meaning
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 1, is the person the Takeover Panel would tell one of the persons specified there` WITH `recipient` IS `sch 2 part 1(B) para 8 a police officer within the meaning of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954`, `the person meets the meaning the entry borrows from another Act` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Part 2 group (A) para 22: a disclosure to enable or assist the Bank of England to exercise its functions.
-- to assist the Bank of England
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 2, is the disclosure the Takeover Panel would make of a specified description` WITH `description` IS `sch 2 part 2(A) para 22 the Bank of England`, `the person or body meets the meaning the description gives to a term` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- to assist nobody Part 2 lists
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 2, is the disclosure the Takeover Panel would make of a specified description` WITH `description` IS `sch 2 part 2 none of the descriptions`, `the person or body meets the meaning the description gives to a term` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Part 2 group (A) para 53: disciplinary proceedings about a public servant, which sub-paragraph (2) defines.
-- disciplinary proceedings about a public servant who is one
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 2, is the disclosure the Takeover Panel would make of a specified description` WITH `description` IS `sch 2 part 2(A) para 53 disciplinary proceedings about a public servant`, `the person or body meets the meaning the description gives to a term` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- disciplinary proceedings about someone who is not a public servant
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 2, is the disclosure the Takeover Panel would make of a specified description` WITH `description` IS `sch 2 part 2(A) para 53 disciplinary proceedings about a public servant`, `the person or body meets the meaning the description gives to a term` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- line 19157 of the text, without its paragraph number
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 2, what are the words of the description` WITH description IS `sch 2 part 2(A) para 22 the Bank of England`) EQUALS "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Bank of England to exercise its functions."
-- Para 52(2): a lawyer is (a) an authorised person for a reserved legal activity (until s 18 of the Legal Services Act 2007 is in force, a solicitor or barrister in England and Wales), (b) a solicitor or barrister in Northern Ireland, (c) a solicitor or advocate in Scotland, (d) a member of a foreign legal profession entitled to practise.
-- section 18 in force; I am an authorised person for a reserved legal activity
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 2 paragraph 52(2), am I a lawyer` WITH `section 18 of the Legal Services Act 2007 has come into force` IS TRUE, `I am an authorised person in relation to an activity that is a reserved legal activity` IS TRUE, `I am a solicitor or barrister in England and Wales` IS FALSE, `I am a solicitor or barrister in Northern Ireland` IS FALSE, `I am a solicitor or advocate in Scotland` IS FALSE, `I am a member of a legal profession regulated outside the United Kingdom` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- section 18 not in force; I am a solicitor in England and Wales
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 2 paragraph 52(2), am I a lawyer` WITH `section 18 of the Legal Services Act 2007 has come into force` IS FALSE, `I am an authorised person in relation to an activity that is a reserved legal activity` IS FALSE, `I am a solicitor or barrister in England and Wales` IS TRUE, `I am a solicitor or barrister in Northern Ireland` IS FALSE, `I am a solicitor or advocate in Scotland` IS FALSE, `I am a member of a legal profession regulated outside the United Kingdom` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I am a solicitor in Northern Ireland
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 2 paragraph 52(2), am I a lawyer` WITH `section 18 of the Legal Services Act 2007 has come into force` IS FALSE, `I am an authorised person in relation to an activity that is a reserved legal activity` IS FALSE, `I am a solicitor or barrister in England and Wales` IS FALSE, `I am a solicitor or barrister in Northern Ireland` IS TRUE, `I am a solicitor or advocate in Scotland` IS FALSE, `I am a member of a legal profession regulated outside the United Kingdom` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I am none of those
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 2 paragraph 52(2), am I a lawyer` WITH `section 18 of the Legal Services Act 2007 has come into force` IS TRUE, `I am an authorised person in relation to an activity that is a reserved legal activity` IS FALSE, `I am a solicitor or barrister in England and Wales` IS FALSE, `I am a solicitor or barrister in Northern Ireland` IS FALSE, `I am a solicitor or advocate in Scotland` IS FALSE, `I am a member of a legal profession regulated outside the United Kingdom` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- para 53(2)(a): an officer or employee of the Crown
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 2 paragraph 53(2), am I a public servant` WITH `I am an officer or employee of the Crown` IS TRUE, `I am an officer or employee of an authority designated by the Secretary of State by order` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- para 53(2)(b): an officer of an authority the Secretary of State has designated by order
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 2 paragraph 53(2), am I a public servant` WITH `I am an officer or employee of the Crown` IS FALSE, `I am an officer or employee of an authority designated by the Secretary of State by order` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- neither limb
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 2 paragraph 53(2), am I a public servant` WITH `I am an officer or employee of the Crown` IS FALSE, `I am an officer or employee of an authority designated by the Secretary of State by order` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Part 3 para 1: made to a body exercising relevant functions overseas, for the purpose of assisting it.
-- to an overseas regulator with public functions that appear similar to the Panel's own, to assist it
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 3 paragraph 1, would the disclosure be made in accordance with Part 3` WITH `the disclosure is made to a person or body exercising functions under legislation in a country or territory outside the British Islands` IS TRUE, `the functions are functions of a public nature` IS TRUE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the Panel's own functions` IS TRUE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to those of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority` IS FALSE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England` IS FALSE, `the disclosure is made for the purpose of enabling or assisting that person or body to exercise those functions` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- to an overseas body, but not made to assist its functions
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 3 paragraph 1, would the disclosure be made in accordance with Part 3` WITH `the disclosure is made to a person or body exercising functions under legislation in a country or territory outside the British Islands` IS TRUE, `the functions are functions of a public nature` IS TRUE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the Panel's own functions` IS TRUE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to those of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority` IS FALSE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England` IS FALSE, `the disclosure is made for the purpose of enabling or assisting that person or body to exercise those functions` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Part 3 para 2: the Panel must have regard to (a) the importance of the use and (b) the recipient's arrangements.
-- deciding; had regard to both
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 3 paragraph 2, has the Takeover Panel had regard to the considerations` WITH `the Panel is determining whether to disclose information to a person or body in accordance with this Part` IS TRUE, `the Panel has had regard to whether the use that the person or body is likely to make of the information is sufficiently important to justify making the disclosure` IS TRUE, `the Panel has had regard to whether the person or body has adequate arrangements to prevent the information from being used or further disclosed otherwise than for the purposes of carrying out the functions mentioned in paragraph 1(1)(a) or for other purposes substantially similar to those for which information disclosed to the Panel could be used or further disclosed` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- deciding; has not had regard to the arrangements
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 3 paragraph 2, has the Takeover Panel had regard to the considerations` WITH `the Panel is determining whether to disclose information to a person or body in accordance with this Part` IS TRUE, `the Panel has had regard to whether the use that the person or body is likely to make of the information is sufficiently important to justify making the disclosure` IS TRUE, `the Panel has had regard to whether the person or body has adequate arrangements to prevent the information from being used or further disclosed otherwise than for the purposes of carrying out the functions mentioned in paragraph 1(1)(a) or for other purposes substantially similar to those for which information disclosed to the Panel could be used or further disclosed` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not deciding whether to disclose under Part 3
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 2 part 3 paragraph 2, has the Takeover Panel had regard to the considerations` WITH `the Panel is determining whether to disclose information to a person or body in accordance with this Part` IS FALSE, `the Panel has had regard to whether the use that the person or body is likely to make of the information is sufficiently important to justify making the disclosure` IS TRUE, `the Panel has had regard to whether the person or body has adequate arrangements to prevent the information from being used or further disclosed otherwise than for the purposes of carrying out the functions mentioned in paragraph 1(1)(a) or for other purposes substantially similar to those for which information disclosed to the Panel could be used or further disclosed` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Schedule 4 -- documents and information you send to your company (or the registrar sends it)`

-- Para 1: applies to documents sent to a company; not to those sent by another company.
-- I send it to my company
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 paragraph 1, does the Schedule apply to the document or information` WITH `the document or information is sent or supplied to a company` IS TRUE, `the document or information is sent or supplied by another company` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- it is sent by another company
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 paragraph 1, does the Schedule apply to the document or information` WITH `the document or information is sent or supplied to a company` IS TRUE, `the document or information is sent or supplied by another company` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- it is not sent to a company at all
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 paragraph 1, does the Schedule apply to the document or information` WITH `the document or information is sent or supplied to a company` IS FALSE, `the document or information is sent or supplied by another company` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Paras 2 to 4: hard copy by hand or by post (a prepaid envelope) to the specified address, the registered office or an address a provision authorises.
-- I hand it in at the registered office
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 paragraph 2, is the paper document I send my company validly sent` WITH `how I send it` IS `sch 4 by hand`, `I post a prepaid envelope containing it` IS FALSE, `the address is one the company specified for the purpose` IS FALSE, `the address is the company's registered office` IS TRUE, `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I post a prepaid envelope to the address the company specified
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 paragraph 2, is the paper document I send my company validly sent` WITH `how I send it` IS `sch 4 by post`, `I post a prepaid envelope containing it` IS TRUE, `the address is one the company specified for the purpose` IS TRUE, `the address is the company's registered office` IS FALSE, `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I post it with no prepaid envelope
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 paragraph 2, is the paper document I send my company validly sent` WITH `how I send it` IS `sch 4 by post`, `I post a prepaid envelope containing it` IS FALSE, `the address is one the company specified for the purpose` IS FALSE, `the address is the company's registered office` IS TRUE, `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I hand it in at an address that is none of the three
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 paragraph 2, is the paper document I send my company validly sent` WITH `how I send it` IS `sch 4 by hand`, `I post a prepaid envelope containing it` IS FALSE, `the address is one the company specified for the purpose` IS FALSE, `the address is the company's registered office` IS FALSE, `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Paras 5 to 7: electronic form needs the company's agreement (or a deemed one) and, by e-mail, an address it specified (or a deemed one).
-- I e-mail it: the company agreed, and I used an address it specified for electronic documents
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 paragraph 5, is the electronic document I send my company validly sent` WITH `how I send it` IS `sch 4 by electronic means`, `the company has agreed that I may send documents in electronic form` IS TRUE, `the company has revoked that agreement` IS FALSE, `a provision of the Companies Acts deems the company to have agreed` IS FALSE, `the address is one the company specified for electronic documents` IS TRUE, `a provision of the Companies Acts deems the address to be specified` IS FALSE, `the address is one the company specified for paper documents` IS FALSE, `the address is the company's registered office` IS FALSE, `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I e-mail it to a specified address but the company never agreed
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 paragraph 5, is the electronic document I send my company validly sent` WITH `how I send it` IS `sch 4 by electronic means`, `the company has agreed that I may send documents in electronic form` IS FALSE, `the company has revoked that agreement` IS FALSE, `a provision of the Companies Acts deems the company to have agreed` IS FALSE, `the address is one the company specified for electronic documents` IS TRUE, `a provision of the Companies Acts deems the address to be specified` IS FALSE, `the address is one the company specified for paper documents` IS FALSE, `the address is the company's registered office` IS FALSE, `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the company agreed but I used an address it did not specify
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 paragraph 5, is the electronic document I send my company validly sent` WITH `how I send it` IS `sch 4 by electronic means`, `the company has agreed that I may send documents in electronic form` IS TRUE, `the company has revoked that agreement` IS FALSE, `a provision of the Companies Acts deems the company to have agreed` IS FALSE, `the address is one the company specified for electronic documents` IS FALSE, `a provision of the Companies Acts deems the address to be specified` IS FALSE, `the address is one the company specified for paper documents` IS FALSE, `the address is the company's registered office` IS FALSE, `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I post a disk to the registered office, the company having agreed
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 paragraph 5, is the electronic document I send my company validly sent` WITH `how I send it` IS `sch 4 by post`, `the company has agreed that I may send documents in electronic form` IS TRUE, `the company has revoked that agreement` IS FALSE, `a provision of the Companies Acts deems the company to have agreed` IS FALSE, `the address is one the company specified for electronic documents` IS FALSE, `a provision of the Companies Acts deems the address to be specified` IS FALSE, `the address is one the company specified for paper documents` IS FALSE, `the address is the company's registered office` IS TRUE, `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Para 4A: from the registrar by electronic means only to a registered company's registered email address, or an address the company specified for that purpose.
-- e-mailed to the registered email address of a company registered under the Act
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 paragraph 4A, was the electronic document the registrar sent my company validly sent` WITH `how it was sent` IS `sch 4 by electronic means`, `the company is registered under this Act` IS TRUE, `it was sent to the company's registered email address` IS TRUE, `it was sent to an address the company specified for that purpose` IS FALSE, `the address is one the company specified for paper documents` IS FALSE, `the address is the company's registered office` IS FALSE, `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- e-mailed to an address that is neither
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 paragraph 4A, was the electronic document the registrar sent my company validly sent` WITH `how it was sent` IS `sch 4 by electronic means`, `the company is registered under this Act` IS TRUE, `it was sent to the company's registered email address` IS FALSE, `it was sent to an address the company specified for that purpose` IS FALSE, `the address is one the company specified for paper documents` IS FALSE, `the address is the company's registered office` IS FALSE, `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a disk posted to the registered office
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 paragraph 4A, was the electronic document the registrar sent my company validly sent` WITH `how it was sent` IS `sch 4 by post`, `the company is registered under this Act` IS FALSE, `it was sent to the company's registered email address` IS FALSE, `it was sent to an address the company specified for that purpose` IS FALSE, `the address is one the company specified for paper documents` IS FALSE, `the address is the company's registered office` IS TRUE, `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the company agreed to that form or manner
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 paragraph 8, is what I send my company in another agreed form validly sent` WITH `the company has agreed that form or manner` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the company did not agree
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 paragraph 8, is what I send my company in another agreed form validly sent` WITH `the company has agreed that form or manner` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Schedule 5 -- documents and information your company sends you`

-- Paras 2 to 4: hard copy must be handed to me, or sent by hand or by post (a prepaid envelope) to an address para 4 allows.
-- the company hands it to me
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 5 paragraph 2, was the paper document my company sent me validly sent` WITH `how the company sent it to me` IS `sch 5 handed to the intended recipient`, `the company posted a prepaid envelope containing it` IS FALSE, `the address is one I specified for the purpose` IS FALSE, `I am a member of the company` IS FALSE, `the address is the one shown for me in the register of members` IS FALSE, `I am a director of the company` IS FALSE, `the address is the one shown for me in the register` IS FALSE, `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS FALSE, `the company could not obtain an address of those kinds` IS FALSE, `the address is my last address known to the company` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- posted in a prepaid envelope to the address I specified
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 5 paragraph 2, was the paper document my company sent me validly sent` WITH `how the company sent it to me` IS `sch 5 by post`, `the company posted a prepaid envelope containing it` IS TRUE, `the address is one I specified for the purpose` IS TRUE, `I am a member of the company` IS FALSE, `the address is the one shown for me in the register of members` IS FALSE, `I am a director of the company` IS FALSE, `the address is the one shown for me in the register` IS FALSE, `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS FALSE, `the company could not obtain an address of those kinds` IS FALSE, `the address is my last address known to the company` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- posted in a prepaid envelope to my address in the register of members, I being a member
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 5 paragraph 2, was the paper document my company sent me validly sent` WITH `how the company sent it to me` IS `sch 5 by post`, `the company posted a prepaid envelope containing it` IS TRUE, `the address is one I specified for the purpose` IS FALSE, `I am a member of the company` IS TRUE, `the address is the one shown for me in the register of members` IS TRUE, `I am a director of the company` IS FALSE, `the address is the one shown for me in the register` IS FALSE, `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS FALSE, `the company could not obtain an address of those kinds` IS FALSE, `the address is my last address known to the company` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- posted in a prepaid envelope to an address that para 4 does not allow
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 5 paragraph 2, was the paper document my company sent me validly sent` WITH `how the company sent it to me` IS `sch 5 by post`, `the company posted a prepaid envelope containing it` IS TRUE, `the address is one I specified for the purpose` IS FALSE, `I am a member of the company` IS FALSE, `the address is the one shown for me in the register of members` IS FALSE, `I am a director of the company` IS FALSE, `the address is the one shown for me in the register` IS FALSE, `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS FALSE, `the company could not obtain an address of those kinds` IS FALSE, `the address is my last address known to the company` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- posted with no prepaid envelope
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 5 paragraph 2, was the paper document my company sent me validly sent` WITH `how the company sent it to me` IS `sch 5 by post`, `the company posted a prepaid envelope containing it` IS FALSE, `the address is one I specified for the purpose` IS TRUE, `I am a member of the company` IS FALSE, `the address is the one shown for me in the register of members` IS FALSE, `I am a director of the company` IS FALSE, `the address is the one shown for me in the register` IS FALSE, `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS FALSE, `the company could not obtain an address of those kinds` IS FALSE, `the address is my last address known to the company` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- sent to my last known address because the company could not obtain another (para 4(2))
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 5 paragraph 2, was the paper document my company sent me validly sent` WITH `how the company sent it to me` IS `sch 5 by post`, `the company posted a prepaid envelope containing it` IS TRUE, `the address is one I specified for the purpose` IS FALSE, `I am a member of the company` IS FALSE, `the address is the one shown for me in the register of members` IS FALSE, `I am a director of the company` IS FALSE, `the address is the one shown for me in the register` IS FALSE, `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS FALSE, `the company could not obtain an address of those kinds` IS TRUE, `the address is my last address known to the company` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Paras 5 to 7: electronic form needs my agreement and an address I specified (or, for a disk, a hard copy address).
-- e-mailed to the address I specified, I having agreed
